add('lola','Route109_Text_LolaPostBattle','Lola compares the beach from above to a flower garden.',
'''soft_smile~Umbrellas are flowers with people growing underneath.|A different viewpoint reveals patterns hidden at ground level.|Makes the crowded colors sound rather peaceful.|I can picture the bright shapes along the sand.|A garden full of picnics is a very good garden.|A beach flowering briefly beneath the sunshine.|Flowers with towels. Remarkably prepared flowers.|Those colors must form a different arrangement from above.|A garden opening with weather and folding by evening.|soft_smile~Everyone's beachwear joins one enormous pattern.|soft_smile~That's exactly the change of viewpoint I'd love to catch.''')
add('lola_rematch','Route109_Text_LolaRematchPostBattle','Lola says a tube makes her and her Pokemon cuter.',
'''soft_smile~A round frame for two very confident faces.|The shared accessory seems part of their enjoyment.|Both happy? Then the tube is doing its job.|She's most pleased when her Pokemon is included.|Matching beach plans can be half the fun.|smug~The tube became director of collective cuteness.|An inflatable endorsement of their existing charm.|One accessory, two delighted users. Efficient design.|They like being a little picture together.|soft_smile~Coordinated silhouettes can improve the whole look.|Sweetest is how she includes her Pokemon in the praise.''')
add('mel','Route109_Text_MelPostBattle','Mel worries that Paul is angry with her.',
'''sad~A lost battle shouldn't leave her afraid to ask that.|I'd rather hear Paul reassure her than guess his mood.|Both battled. She needn't carry all of it.|sad~Her voice changed there. I hope he answers gently.|A kind word from Paul would beat any battle advice.|They need this conversation without extra pressure from us.|A small question holding an uncomfortable amount of worry.|They need to talk before planning another match.|She should be able to ask without bracing for the answer.|Give them space to answer each other honestly.|I'd hear Paul's answer before making this into a joke.''')
add('paul','Route109_Text_PaulPostBattle','Paul asks for privacy on his beach visit with Mel.',
'''soft_smile~A world of two with unexpectedly competitive visitors.|We can respect privacy without making a spectacle of it.|Fine. We'll leave them to their afternoon.|I don't mind keeping a quiet outing quiet.|They can enjoy themselves. There's plenty of beach.|A world of two with one brief guest appearance.|soft_smile~My talent for not announcing things proves useful.|No announcement required. Let's give them space.|A little privacy costs us nothing at all.|We needn't turn their outing into local news.|Some moments belong to the people in them.''')
add('ricky','Route109_Text_RickyPostBattle','Ricky is hungry enough to mistake his tube for a doughnut.',
'''laughing~Lunch, before he discovers the disappointing filling.|Hunger has changed his interpretation of equipment.|Feed him before the tube becomes evidence.|Now he said it, I can't unsee that doughnut.|soft_smile~Let's find something with a less rubbery finish.|An excellent shape with entirely wrong ingredients.|An inflatable pastry. Appearance without consolation.|surprised~That tube isn't rated for this particular emergency.|Hunger gives the imagination strong powers of suggestion.|The silhouette works. The texture would be unforgivable.|His face when he saw it says enough about lunchtime.''')
add('ricky_rematch','Route109_Text_RickyRematchPostBattle','Ricky thinks beach food tastes better.',
'''soft_smile~Sand nearby is the secret. Not sand inside.|Setting and appetite change how enjoyable food feels.|Food after a long swim earns the praise.|A plain snack feels special with the water in front.|soft_smile~Picnics improve when you aren't fighting the wind.|Fine atmosphere. Very questionable table service.|A sandwich with a view. Skip the geological seasoning.|Good company and a securely closed lunch box help.|Sometimes a place becomes part of a remembered taste.|smug~Agreed, provided the beach stays outside the sandwich.|I remember who I ate with as much as the food.''')
add('abigail','Route110_Text_AbigailPostBattle','Abigail needs proper rest after exhausting herself.',
'''soft_smile~Her legs voted for a recess. Sensible legs.|Recognizing fatigue is part of managing exertion.|Good call. Take the break you need.|She sounds relieved to admit she needs a pause.|A seat and something to drink would help that break.|An intermission with no need for an apology.|A compelling argument for remaining seated.|Stopping now might prevent a much longer forced stop later.|Rest belongs in a journey, not outside it.|She can have a break without earning it twice.|I'd rather chat when she has caught her breath.''')
add('abigail_rematch','Route110_Text_AbigailRematchPostBattle','Abigail apologizes for interrupting a possible record attempt.',
'''smug~Our bicycle did not submit a record application.|She needn't assume every rider is measuring a fastest time.|No harm done. We chose to battle.|I'd rather enjoy the road than worry about a stopwatch.|A friendly stop isn't wasted time to me.|Not every journey requires a triumphant numerical conclusion.|smug~My personal record for unnecessary rushing remains safe.|A timed attempt would call for planning around interruptions.|She has mistaken our progress for urgency.|An apology is kind, but this was a welcome diversion.|Meeting people is a reason to travel this road too.''')
add('alyssa','Route110_Text_AlyssaPostBattle','Alyssa is humiliated by falling and losing.',
'''That was a rough pair of events. No encore needed.|Two setbacks close together can feel larger than they are.|Check she's all right before discussing the loss.|I wouldn't want people staring after a fall either.|A quiet break could help more than cheerful advice.|She needn't turn one bad afternoon into her entire story.|Embarrassment has a cruel habit of inviting an audience.|First make sure nothing hurts beyond her pride.|Let her gather herself without another demand.|We can give her dignity by not making a spectacle.|I'd lower the attention rather than capture the moment.''')
add('anthony','Route110_Text_AnthonyPostBattle','Anthony realizes speed alone cannot win.',
'''Fast enough to reach the problem ahead of his solution.|Speed is useful within a plan, not in place of one.|Quick feet don't choose the right move.|Slowing down might let him notice what he missed.|He can keep the speed and add some thought.|He arrived at the conclusion at a commendable pace.|At least the realization did not require a lap.|A fast system still needs sensible control.|Haste can carry us past what we needed to see.|One excellent feature rarely completes the entire design.|He noticed the limit himself. That's a better start than another burst of speed.''')
