add('benjamin','Route110_Text_BenjaminPostBattle Route110_Text_BenjaminRematchPostBattle','Benjamin encourages an unhurried approach.',
'''soft_smile~At last, permission to stop racing our own shoes.|An unhurried decision can be more accurate than a panicked one.|Steady works. No need to make extra trouble.|soft_smile~It's nice hearing that we don't have to rush.|We can take a proper break without abandoning the trip.|The road has declined to impose a dramatic deadline.|A pace my lungs can endorse without amendments.|Enough time to check a plan beats rushing into repairs.|A calm step still carries us forward.|I appreciate an invitation without a hidden stopwatch.|We might notice more if we give this road some time.''')
add('dale','Route110_Text_DalePostBattle','Dale says fishing requires focus on the float.',
'''One tiny float has secured his undivided attention.|Small changes are easier to detect with sustained observation.|Watch the float. Don't let us distract you.|That much stillness takes more attention than it looks.|I could keep the lunch ready while he watches.|The most important actor here barely moves.|A tiny object with a demanding social schedule.|A clear indicator is useful only if someone monitors it.|Patience sometimes means attending closely, not drifting away.|Such a little point to organize an entire afternoon around.|I'd watch his face for the instant the float changes.''')
add('edward','Route110_Text_EdwardPostBattle','Edward predicts a shining light in our future.',
'''surprised~Wonderful. I was worried we would need another lamp.|That prediction is rather broad. I'd ask what he means.|A light ahead. Hopefully a clear path under it.|A bright future is a nice thought, even stated vaguely.|I'll take encouragement without asking it to plan dinner.|smug~A luminous prophecy with admirably flexible interpretation.|At least my future has adequate visibility.|I'd like details before designing anything around the forecast.|Some lights guide; others simply ask us to look.|An intriguing promise. I prefer to help make it happen.|A shining light could describe so many things. His expression makes it feel hopeful.''')
add('edwin','Route110_Text_EdwinPostBattle','Unfamiliar Pokemon excite Edwin\'s collecting interests.',
'''surprised~His curiosity just spotted an empty space in its collection.|An unfamiliar species can be an excellent reason to learn.|New Pokemon. Plenty to learn before catching one.|The excitement in his voice changed straightaway.|Learning what it needs should be part of meeting it.|His catalogue has discovered the thrill of an unfinished page.|An unknown Pokemon. His afternoon now has a purpose.|I'd start by observing what makes it different.|The unfamiliar can draw us closer without belonging to us.|A new face has completely revived his interest.|soft_smile~An unfamiliar face has pulled his attention right past the battle result.''')
add('edwin_rematch','Route110_Text_EdwinRematchPostBattle','Edwin longs to own every rare Pokemon.',
'''Every rare one? His storage plans must be enormous.|Rarity says little about the care a Pokemon will require.|Wanting one isn't the same as being ready for it.|I wonder which one he likes beyond its rarity.|Each new Pokemon needs more than a space on a list.|A sweeping ambition. Every individual still deserves a proper welcome.|A collection that would make quiet afternoons difficult.|I'd calculate the care requirements before the display capacity.|A rare life remains a life, not merely a missing entry.|A good collection should reflect attention, not just acquisition.|The rare ones are exciting, but I hope the familiar ones still catch his eye.''')
add('isabel','Route110_Text_IsabelPostBattle','Isabel considers showing off at the Fan Club instead of battling.',
'''smug~An audience that applauds instead of attacking. Smart adjustment.|Admiring Pokemon needn't always involve testing their strength.|Fan Club sounds like a better fit today.|She might enjoy being able to show them without pressure.|A happy team has plenty worth celebrating outside battles.|She has located a more appreciative set of critics.|A gathering where nobody faints from the reviews. Usually.|Different venues reward different qualities. Worth trying both.|Affection does not need a contest to be visible.|soft_smile~She could find people delighted by the details she loves.|She wants someone to see what she sees in her Pokemon. The Fan Club might understand.''')
add('isabel_rematch','Route110_Text_IsabelRematchPostBattle','Isabel enjoys both showing off Pokemon and battling.',
'''She wants the applause and the action. A complete outing.|She needn't choose between admiration and competition.|Likes both. Plenty of room for that.|Her fondness comes through even when she's being competitive.|There can be time for showing off between matches.|A devoted admirer who also insists on a lively plot.|She has more than one way to embarrass her Pokemon lovingly.|A battle can reveal qualities a quiet display misses.|She has found two ways to enjoy the same company.|Of course she can enjoy both. One good look deserves movement.|I'd like to see which little habits she points out afterward.''')
add('jaclyn','Route110_Text_JaclynPostBattle','Jaclyn dismisses our victory as a miracle.',
'''smug~A miracle! Our practice will be delighted to hear it.|One outcome alone cannot support her confident explanation.|She can call it luck. We still won.|It hurts to lose. I wouldn't argue the label right now.|She can be disappointed without taking our effort away.|A wonder so convenient it explains away every detail.|smug~Our hard work has apparently joined the supernatural.|Reviewing the actual moves would explain more than insisting.|Sometimes pride makes an ordinary result seem impossible.|She is dressing disappointment in an elaborate excuse.|I'd be curious what she noticed once the frustration faded.''')
add('jacob','Route110_Text_JacobPostBattle','Jacob warns us to inspect bike tires and brakes.',
'''Our bike deserves a check before the road checks it for us.|Tires and brakes are worth inspecting before a long ride.|Good advice. Check before the downhill stretch.|I'd rather stop for a check than for a fall.|A short pause now can save a painful walk later.|An unglamorous precaution with an excellent survival record.|I prefer my dramatic stops to remain theoretical.|Absolutely. Loose brakes don't improve through optimism.|Care for what carries us is part of the journey.|Scuffed pride is easier to fix than a bad fall.|We can look at the bike before admiring the next view.''')
add('jasmine','Route110_Text_JasminePostBattle','Jasmine attributes our strength to Gym Badges.',
'''soft_smile~The badges are little shiny receipts for a lot of effort.|They record successful challenges, though not all the practice.|Earned them the hard way. They don't do the fighting.|She noticed the part we can carry on our clothes.|There's a lot of work packed into those small badges.|An impressive credential with a less polished history behind it.|Our suffering has acquired tasteful metal documentation.|Evidence of progress, not a replacement for preparation.|Small objects can hold the weight of long efforts.|They do give a useful first impression.|I'd tell her about a battle behind one of those badges.''')
add('joseph','Route110_Text_JosephPostBattle','Joseph insists losing has improved him.',
'''That loss has been hired as a personal instructor.|A useful response, if he can identify what he learned.|Good. Put that lesson into the next fight.|I like that he hasn't let it flatten his enthusiasm.|He sounds ready to try again after a proper break.|Defeat has been given a surprisingly positive reference.|A loss with career development opportunities. Unexpected.|I'd ask which adjustment he wants to try first.|He is leaving with more than the result alone.|Confidence looks better when it can survive a setback.|I'd like to see what changes next time he battles.''')
add('kaleb','Route110_Text_KalebPostBattle','Kaleb reassures his Pokemon they did their best.',
'''soft_smile~Their trainer kept the compliment when the victory got away.|Acknowledging effort gives the team more than blame would.|Good. Don't make the team carry his disappointment.|soft_smile~That was a gentle way to end a rough match.|They worked hard. A little kindness afterward matters.|A gracious closing line for the ones who did the fighting.|His pretties have retained their title despite the score.|Encouragement first; adjustments can wait until they're rested.|They can rest without fearing they have lost his affection.|That is a much nicer reception than scolding tired Pokemon.|soft_smile~I noticed how his attention went straight back to them.''')
add('timmy','Route110_Text_TimmyPostBattle','Timmy struggles to battle with recently caught Pokemon.',
'''Introductions first, victory speeches later.|A new partnership needs time to establish reliable communication.|Get to know them. Then ask for more.|It must be awkward before you understand each other's timing.|Spend ordinary time together too, not just difficult battles.|A new cast needs more than one hurried rehearsal.|Strangers rarely become coordinated because someone shouts harder.|Start with simple situations and learn how they respond.|Trust does not appear at the instant of a catch.|A team needs a relationship beyond looking good together.|The first little habits you notice can become the ones you remember longest.''')
add('beau','Route111_Text_BeauPostBattle','Beau will train with his Pokemon to become a hero.',
'''Hero training begins with getting back up, apparently.|His plan includes improving himself alongside his Pokemon.|Good heroes put the work in with their team.|I like that he says both of them will grow stronger.|Being kind on an ordinary day is useful practice too.|A promising origin story, provided he keeps doing the work.|An ambitious title. At least he has a training plan.|Small, repeatable goals could make that big ambition practical.|A hero can begin by caring for the partner beside him.|He has the confidence. Now comes the less glamorous effort.|He sounds excited about becoming someone, not just winning something.''')
add('becky','Route111_Text_BeckyPostBattle','Becky infers a former sea from desert fossils.',
'''surprised~The desert kept the sea's old belongings.|soft_smile~Fossils can preserve evidence of environments very different from today.|Hard to picture water here. The fossils make a case.|That makes the dry landscape feel strangely deeper.|A place can change entirely and still keep traces.|The desert has an unexpectedly maritime backstory.|An ocean replaced by sand. A very thorough redecorating.|I'd like to know which fossils led her to that conclusion.|Dry earth can remember water for a very long time.|A dramatic change, with a few old details left behind.|surprised~I'd love to compare the fossils with this view.''')
add('bianca','Route111_Text_BiancaPostBattle','Bianca points out the long road ahead.',
'''Good thing the road isn't charging us by the step.|A long route is easier to manage with sensible stopping points.|Then we'll pace ourselves. No point burning out.|It looks less daunting when I think about the next stop.|We should check supplies before adding more miles.|A long journey still consists of one manageable stretch at a time.|The road has made a convincing argument for comfortable shoes.|We can plan the next rest before we need it badly.|There is no need to carry the whole distance at once.|A long road deserves practical shoes and realistic expectations.|That long view makes each little place to stop feel more important.''')
add('branden','Route111_Text_BrandenPostBattle','Branden says Sandshrew loves eating his sandwiches.',
'''laughing~Sandshrew has discovered the true purpose of a packed lunch.|Its enthusiasm is clear. I wonder which ingredients it prefers.|Pack an extra. That sandwich has competition.|It's sweet that he knows that little preference.|soft_smile~He should pack a suitable little portion just for Sandshrew.|A lunch thief with an unusually affectionate defense.|A creature after my heart, and apparently his lunch.|A separate container could prevent surprise sandwich shortages.|Sharing food leaves a small, familiar kind of memory.|soft_smile~That sandwich is clearly the most popular item in his bag.|I'd like to see Sandshrew's face when lunch comes out.''')
add('brooke','Route111_Text_BrookePostBattle','Brooke feels her diligent Pokemon training still needs work.',
'''Her hard work didn't vanish because we found room for more.|Diligence and opportunities to improve can exist together.|The effort counts. Now she knows where to adjust.|It must sting after she's tried so carefully.|She can keep the good habits and change the parts that failed.|One rough review does not invalidate the whole manuscript.|Being unfinished is annoyingly compatible with working hard.|A specific adjustment would help more than condemning all her work.|Care can remain steady while methods change.|She needn't throw out everything because one result disappointed her.|She sounds more disappointed because she genuinely cares about doing this well.''')
add('bryan','Route111_Text_BryanPostBattle','Bryan describes mysteries hidden in shifting desert sands.',
'''The sand keeps rearranging its filing system.|Shifting terrain can expose evidence and conceal it again.|Then watch your bearings while looking for them.|It feels strange knowing the view won't stay this way.|A search like that needs water as well as curiosity.|A mystery whose scenery refuses to stay in position.|The desert has inconvenient habits for an archivist.|Recording where a discovery appeared could be tricky here.|Some places keep their stories beneath a moving blanket.|An intriguing place, with a very uncooperative backdrop.|The sand makes everything look temporary, even when something ancient lies beneath it.''')
add('celia','Route111_Text_CeliaPostBattle','Celia cannot set a picnic in the sandstorm even with goggles.',
'''smug~The goggles protect her eyes, not the sandwiches.|Eye protection doesn't solve the problem of airborne sand in food.|Find shelter. Don't picnic in the storm.|Trying to keep every plate covered sounds exhausting.|annoyed~A sheltered spot would save the meal and everyone's patience.|The picnic requires less atmosphere, in a rather literal sense.|annoyed~The desert has supplied an unwanted seasoning.|The whole setup needs shelter, not a better pair of goggles.|A meal deserves somewhere the wind won't keep taking it.|The setting is impressive. The table service is hostile.|I'd help her find somewhere the food stays recognizable.''')
add('celina','Route111_Text_CelinaPostBattle','Celina is excited and impressed after our battle.',
'''surprised~Our battle has apparently become a cardiovascular event.|The excitement can linger after the match has ended.|Take a breath. That was a good match.|soft_smile~She sounds delighted rather than upset about losing.|A drink and a quiet minute might suit that racing pulse.|An enthusiastic review delivered before the excitement has settled.|A compliment with its own percussion section.|Let's give her a moment to catch her breath.|Some encounters leave their warmth in us awhile.|She makes a sincere compliment wonderfully easy to accept.|Her excitement makes the match sound worth remembering from both sides.''')
add('daisuke','Route111_Text_DaisukePostBattle','Daisuke intends to keep training against strong trainers.',
'''His next plan is more practice. Sturdy construction.|Focused practice helps more than repeating the same attempt blindly.|Keep at it. Rest the team between tries.|He seems determined without sounding bitter.|Training works better when the team is ready to enjoy it.|Defeat has supplied him with a target rather than an ending.|Persistence is less flashy than talent and harder to lose.|He could start with the move that disrupted his plan.|A patient effort can outlast an intimidating opponent.|He has the resolve. Small improvements will give it shape.|I'd like to see what he changes before our next match.''')
add('drew','Route111_Text_DrewPostBattle','Drew is happy goggles let him travel through sandstorms.',
'''A tiny window for each eye, and suddenly more desert.|Suitable equipment can make a difficult environment accessible.|Good gear. Still watch the rest of the weather.|It must feel good to see where he's going again.|That makes a hard trip less miserable at least.|A change of eyewear has expanded his entire itinerary.|Fashion that keeps the landscape out of your eyelashes.|A simple protective design doing exactly what it should.|A little clear space between his eyes and the storm.|Practical eyewear earns its place in this outfit.|Being able to look into the storm must change how the whole desert feels.''')
add('dusty','Route111_Text_DustyPostBattle','Dusty forgets whether he searched for ruins for thirty or forty years.',
'''surprised~Even the search has become an ancient mystery.|That is a long commitment, whichever decade is correct.|Long enough to earn a rest in the shade.|I wonder which discovery he remembers most clearly.|He must have plenty of stories from those years.|smug~His expedition has developed its own disputed chronology.|A decade wandered off. The desert does conceal things.|A dated field journal would help settle that question.|Years blur, while certain stones remain distinct.|The exact number matters less than what kept drawing him back.|There must be particular days that stand out even when the decades blur.''')
add('hayden','Route111_Text_HaydenPostBattle','Hungry Hayden considers grilling Berries.',
'''A grumbling stomach has submitted a cooking proposal.|I wonder which Berries he has available for grilling.|Find a suitable spot before lighting anything.|Warm Berries sound lovely after all this walking.|Some Berries soften beautifully with gentle heat.|The menu has been dictated by a very vocal audience.|The stomach is an editor with extremely clear demands.|A controlled heat source and a steady surface would help.|A warm meal could make this dry place kinder.|That plan sounds promising, provided the Berries survive the enthusiasm.|I'd like to know what he usually cooks out here.''')
add('heidi','Route111_Text_HeidiPostBattle','Heidi warns sandstorms can wear down battling Pokemon.',
'''The sand insists on joining battles without an invitation.|Environmental damage can matter even between the obvious attacks.|Watch the whole fight, not just the opponent.|It's easy to focus on one hit and miss the slow harm.|A quick check afterward would be kind to the team.|An adversary in every direction, with very little dramatic restraint.|The weather has terrible manners and excellent persistence.|Repeated small damage can become the deciding problem.|The air itself can ask too much of a tired creature.|Even a good strategy needs to account for the setting.|I'd watch how the team is coping between turns.''')
add('irene','Route111_Text_IrenePostBattle','Irene considers Mt. Chimney but enjoys the current view.',
'''The next view has competition from this one.|There is no harm in observing this landscape before moving on.|Mountain will wait. Enjoy the stop.|I know that feeling of not wanting to leave a view.|We could have a little break before choosing the next climb.|A destination needn't steal all the attention from the way there.|A pleasant case of scenery interrupting ambition.|A short pause might make the onward decision easier.|Some places ask us to remain a little longer.|She can enjoy this view without canceling the next one.|She keeps looking around as if the decision has already partly made itself.''')
add('travis','Route111_Text_TravisPostBattle','Travis notices energetic trainers.',
'''Our pep has become a visible roadside attraction.|Enthusiasm is often apparent in posture and movement.|Hard to miss someone charging down a road.|Energy does make someone stand out in a quiet place.|I hope the energy lasts until we find lunch.|An entrance needn't be deliberate to catch someone's eye.|I will continue my research into being less noticeable.|He seems interested in how trainers carry themselves.|A lively presence changes the feel of a place.|Confidence can be visible before anyone says a word.|He seems to notice the energy people bring into a place, not just their team.''')
add('tyron','Route111_Text_TyronPostBattle','Tyron assumes all trainers enjoy showing off their Pokemon.',
'''Some show off. Others are trying to remember the plan.|Trainers can enjoy the same battle for different reasons.|Some do. Some just want a good fight.|I get shy about showing off, even when I'm proud.|I'm happiest when the team seems comfortable and engaged.|He enjoys the audience; others might prefer the contest.|I enjoy a battle that doesn't require announcing my feelings.|Demonstrating what a team learned can be satisfying.|Pride can be quiet as well as visible.|Showing off is fun when the Pokemon seem happy to join in.|He wants everyone to see the things he's proud of. Not everyone enjoys that same spotlight.''')
add('vicky','Route111_Text_VickyPostBattle','Vicky invites us to spend time with the family.',
'''soft_smile~An invitation with no running attached. Very tempting.|A relaxed conversation could tell us more than another match.|A short visit sounds all right to me.|soft_smile~It's kind of her to leave room for us to stay.|soft_smile~I'd gladly sit awhile if nobody is being put out.|A welcome that doesn't demand a grand occasion.|I can socialize briefly if sitting down is involved.|We can spare time to hear how everyone's doing.|A little hospitality can make the road feel less long.|That sounds warmer than hurrying straight away.|I'd enjoy hearing more about the family when they're relaxed.''')
add('wilton','Route111_Text_WiltonPostBattle','Wilton says Pokemon and trainers learn from battles and losses.',
'''A lost match can still leave useful things in your bag.|Trainer and Pokemon both contribute to what changes afterward.|Learn the lesson. Come back prepared.|It helps when losing isn't treated like the end.|Try again after giving the team a proper rest.|Persistence gives an unhappy chapter a chance to lead somewhere.|Failure with notes is slightly less infuriating.|He could identify one thing to improve before repeating the attempt.|An ending can become a place to begin more carefully.|I like that he includes the trainer in the learning.|He includes himself in the lesson. That makes the advice feel fairer to his Pokemon.''')
add('brice','Route112_Text_BricePostBattle','Brice laughs and sneezes after something enters his nose.',
'''laughing~His laugh has acquired a surprise percussion instrument.|That sneeze seems to have interrupted a very good mood.|Let the man sneeze before asking questions.|soft_smile~I nearly laughed too, though he sounds uncomfortable.|A clean cloth might be more useful than our commentary.|A cheerful speech with an involuntary final flourish.|An unexpected nasal plot twist. These things happen.|He should clear that irritation before drawing another huge breath.|The mountain has found a very direct way to interrupt.|Laughter is lovely. Breathing comfortably is lovelier.|That expression changed from laughter to surprise very quickly.''')
add('bryant','Route112_Text_BryantPostBattle','Bryant compliments our battle flair.',
'''Flair! I knew the extra dramatic blinking would pay off.|He noticed how the decisions fit together, not just the result.|Good to hear. Style worked this time.|It's nice when someone notices the way you do something.|A little confidence can make practiced moves feel natural.|A critic of taste as well as a fellow competitor.|Our awkward practice has apparently developed an aesthetic.|A working plan can look surprisingly elegant in motion.|A familiar skill sometimes takes on a shape of its own.|An effective battle with a little personality. Strong combination.|He noticed something personal in the way we battled. That's a lovely kind of attention.''')
add('carol','Route112_Text_CarolPostBattle','Carol values enjoyment over skill in singing and Pokemon.',
'''soft_smile~A contest where smiling is a winning strategy. I qualify.|Enjoyment can be worthwhile without an external ranking.|Having fun counts. Keep treating the team well.|soft_smile~Singing without worrying whether it's good sounds freeing.|A shared good time can be worth more than the score.|She has designed a competition with wonderfully generous rules.|A low-pressure invitation to be publicly imperfect.|Enjoying practice makes it easier to return to it.|A joyful thing needn't prove itself to remain joyful.|She gives everyone room to try without looking polished.|I'd love to hear the song she enjoys most.''')
add('larry','Route112_Text_LarryPostBattle','Larry denies crying because he misses his mother.',
'''soft_smile~He needn't win the argument about why his eyes are wet.|Missing someone familiar is nothing to be ashamed of.|No need to explain. Take a minute.|sad~He can miss her without having to tell us.|We could ask if he needs help getting somewhere familiar.|His dignity can survive without a convincing denial.|I've also blamed my eyes on convenient weather.|A practical offer of help might be easier to accept.|Homesickness can arrive even on a bright day.|Let him keep his explanation if it makes this easier.|He might accept some company more easily than a question about his tears.''')
add('shayla','Route112_Text_ShaylaPostBattle','Shayla tentatively asks for an immediate rematch.',
'''soft_smile~She has wrapped a battle challenge in very soft packaging.|It's considerate to leave us room to decline.|No pressure. Another time is fine too.|flustered~That sounds like the way I'd ask something I really wanted.|We should make sure both teams are ready before another match.|An invitation with an unusually graceful escape clause.|A challenge that respects my calendar. Rare and welcome.|A quick condition check would decide whether another round makes sense.|She makes room for our answer alongside her wish.|She wants a rematch without making a demand. Nicely done.|I'd rather give her an honest answer than leave her guessing.''')
add('trent','Route112_Text_TrentPostBattle','Trent recommends strenuous hiking with a heavy pack.',
'''His fitness plan includes carrying half the mountain up itself.|A training load should match the hiker's ability and conditions.|Build up to it. Don't wreck your knees proving a point.|That sounds more demanding than the walk I had planned.|A heavy pack still needs water and sensible breaks.|A formidable itinerary, though not compulsory for every traveler.|My bag already feels sufficiently invested in my suffering.|Pack fit and gradual increases matter more than impressive weight.|The mountain need not be conquered in a single burdened climb.|I'll favor a comfortable fit over a dramatic load.|He makes that load sound ordinary. It probably took time before it felt that way.''')
add('trent_rematch','Route112_Text_TrentRematchPostBattle','Trent wants to challenge tough trainers on Mt. Chimney.',
'''The climb ends with more fighting. His legs must be thrilled.|He has found a clear destination for his training goals.|Reach the top with enough left for the battle.|That sounds exciting if he can catch his breath first.|He should save some energy for whoever he meets.|A summit with both a view and a formidable guest list.|His reward for climbing is apparently further exertion.|Supplies should account for the climb and the challenge afterward.|Ambition has found a high place to stand.|He'll want practical gear, not just an impressive entrance.|I'd like to hear how those summit battles go for him.''')
add('coby','Route113_Text_CobyPostBattle','Coby cannot find words after an easy defeat.',
'''No speech required. The scoreboard already talked plenty.|He needn't explain a result before he has processed it.|Take a breath. Nobody needs an excuse.|Silence after losing doesn't have to be awkward.|A quiet rest might help more than finding the perfect words.|No rule requires a polished closing remark from the defeated.|I support not knowing what to say. It happens often.|We could discuss the difficult turn later, when he's ready.|Some feelings need a little time before words arrive.|He can keep his dignity without composing an explanation.|I'd give him a moment instead of filling the silence.''')
add('dillon','Route113_Text_DillonPostBattle','Dillon jokes about ash in his eyelashes then apologizes.',
'''laughing~That joke got in my eyes too. Mostly from laughing.|Wordplay is less enjoyable with actual grit in one's eyes.|Clear your eyes first. Apologize for the joke later.|soft_smile~I smiled. I just wish it hadn't hurt to discover the rhyme.|Let's deal with the ash before reviewing his comedy.|A painful setup with an apologetic punchline.|I forgive the joke. The ash remains under suspicion.|A clean rinse is more urgent than improving that pun.|Even an unfortunate moment can leave a small joke behind.|smug~His delivery needed less volcanic material.|The apology was almost funnier than the original joke.''')
add('jaylen','Route113_Text_JaylenPostBattle','Jaylen enjoys the cooler weather under volcanic ash.',
'''The sun got a curtain and he got his preferred afternoon.|Ash can reduce incoming sunlight. Comfort is only one effect.|Cooler suits him. Still watch the ash.|I like cooler air too, though this is an unusual way to get it.|A comfortable temperature makes walking much easier.|His ideal weather arrived wearing a rather ominous disguise.|A dimmer sky with practical benefits. I understand the appeal.|Reduced sunlight changes the conditions beyond temperature too.|He has found relief beneath an unlikely shade.|The ash makes a dramatic canopy, but I prefer cleaner shade.|The dim light is part of why he feels at home here. I'd never have guessed that first.''')
add('lao','Route113_Text_LaoPostBattle','Lao departs to improve his concealment.',
'''His farewell may be the most visible part of his technique.|A failed concealment attempt gives him information to refine.|We spotted him. Now he knows what to fix.|He made leaving sound rather graceful despite the loss.|A little rest before hiding again wouldn't hurt.|A formal farewell from someone professionally opposed to being noticed.|His disappearance has been helpfully announced.|I'd examine which movement or outline gave him away.|The shadow can receive him without an argument.|A quieter outfit might help more than a grand farewell.|I'd be curious what first made him visible to us.''')
add('lawrence','Route113_Text_LawrencePostBattle','Lawrence considers hiding under the ash.',
'''An ash blanket sounds terrible for keeping laundry clean.|Concealment isn't the only concern when choosing a hiding place.|Find somewhere you can breathe comfortably.|It looks like a lonely, uncomfortable place to wait.|I'd choose shelter that doesn't get into every mouthful.|A dramatic disappearance with an unfortunate cleaning bill.|I enjoy gloomy surroundings. Being buried is excessive.|A hiding spot needs visibility and a clear way out too.|He can find quiet without becoming part of the ground.|That would be an ambitious commitment to the local palette.|He seems to like the idea of vanishing more than the reality of lying in ash.''')
add('lung','Route113_Text_LungPostBattle','Lung says hiding becomes lonely when nobody comes.',
'''A perfect hiding spot can be a terrible place to meet people.|His goal of concealment conflicts with his wish for company.|Come out awhile. People can find you then.|sad~That sounds lonelier than he meant it to sound.|He could join us for a little break in the open.|The invisible hero has discovered a shortage of visitors.|sad~I understand wanting quiet until it becomes too quiet.|Maybe set a time to emerge even if nobody finds him.|A hidden place can stop feeling kind when we stay too long.|Mystery is fun until nobody knows you're there.|soft_smile~I'd rather talk to him where he doesn't have to wait unseen.''')
add('madeline','Route113_Text_MadelinePostBattle','Madeline is impressed by our skill.',
'''A good review and no ash in the compliments.|She seems to have watched the match thoughtfully.|Kind of her. She gave us a proper fight.|That sounded sincere. It makes the practice feel worth it.|It's pleasant when a hard match ends warmly.|An appreciative opponent makes a victory easier to enjoy.|A compliment delivered without threatening a rematch. Refreshing.|I'd like to know which decision impressed her.|A little recognition can warm a gray afternoon.|She makes losing look rather gracious.|Her compliment feels like she really watched, rather than just noticed who won.''')
add('sophie','Route113_Text_SophiePostBattle','Sophie angrily decides to sleep after losing.',
'''smug~Her anger has been referred to the nap department.|A rest may help, though this isn't an ideal sleeping spot.|Don't sleep somewhere unsafe just to make a point.|She sounds upset enough to want the whole day to stop.|Somewhere comfortable would be better for that nap.|A furious exit achieved without moving an inch.|smug~Spite sleeping. I recognize the basic technique.|I'd at least check the ground before powering down.|Rest should shelter her, not simply end the conversation.|Even an angry nap deserves a decent location.|I'd let her cool down without giving her more attention.''')
add('tia','Route113_Text_TiaPostBattle','Tia believes they gathered enough ash for a White Flute.',
'''They turned a very dusty walk into a musical budget.|A clear goal makes the amount collected more meaningful.|Good haul. Check before carrying any more.|I'd love to hear what the finished flute sounds like.|A worthwhile reward for hauling all that ash.|The dusty expedition may finally have earned its instrument.|An elegant future for something currently in everyone's shoes.|They should compare the amount with the maker's requirement.|A gray handful can become something with a clear voice.|That's a lovely transformation from a messy raw material.|I'd like to see the flute once their collection becomes one.''')
add('tori','Route113_Text_ToriPostBattle','Tori is unsure if they have enough ash for a White Flute.',
'''This expedition needs a counting pause before more dust.|Checking the required amount would settle that uncertainty.|Measure first. No sense guessing with a full bag.|She sounds hopeful. I hope they're nearly there.|They could ask before making another long collecting trip.|Suspense has appeared at the bottom of an ash bag.|A question with an unusually dusty answer.|A simple estimate could prevent hauling far more than needed.|It is easier to carry a burden when its end is visible.|The flute sounds worth checking the collection carefully.|She's picturing the finished flute while they're still carrying its dusty beginning.''')
add('wyatt','Route113_Text_WyattPostBattle','Wyatt assumes we are gloating after his loss.',
'''We came to talk, not polish our victory on him.|He may be interpreting attention through his disappointment.|No need to rub it in. We can leave.|I wouldn't want him thinking we came over just to laugh.|He can have a little space without another argument.|A villainous motive has been assigned to an ordinary conversation.|My awkward small talk is many things. Triumphal is ambitious.|We can let him cool off rather than argue over intent.|A sore moment can make even a greeting feel sharp.|I won't turn his bad mood into a public contest.|I'd try again when conversation doesn't feel like another battle.''')
add('angelina','Route114_Text_AngelinaPostBattle','Angelina finds dramatic Pokemon evolution startling.',
'''Same friend, startling new packaging.|Evolution can produce remarkable changes in form and behavior.|Give them time to get used to the change.|I wonder if familiar habits make the new shape feel less strange.|Knowing the same little preferences would be comforting.|A transformation with the original relationship still inside.|A dramatic change without needing a new introduction.|I'd be curious which abilities change alongside the shape.|A familiar life can arrive in an unfamiliar outline.|A complete new silhouette, with your old friend looking out.|I'd watch for the small habits that stay the same.''')
# Reviewed byte-identical post-rematch aliases below retain the same conversation.
add('bernie','Route114_Text_BerniePostBattle Route114_Text_BerniePostRematch','Bernie warns against underestimating fire in a forest.',
'''A tiny fire can become a very large problem.|Dry vegetation can let a small ignition spread quickly.|He's right. Be careful with any flame here.|The forest sounds peaceful. I'd like it to stay that way.|Cooking can wait until we find a suitable place.|Fire needn't be dramatic to deserve our full attention.|A warning I am happy to leave entirely untested.|Control the surroundings before introducing a heat source.|The living wood deserves more care than confidence.|A beautiful setting is no excuse to take that risk.|I'd check the ground and branches before anyone lights anything.''')
add('charlotte','Route114_Text_CharlottePostBattle','Charlotte likes cute Pokemon with quirks.',
'''Cute with a surprise feature. My favorite category.|Individual behavior often becomes more interesting than appearance.|A little personality makes good company.|The odd habits are often what I get fondest of.|The fussy little preferences make them feel like family.|A charming face improves with an unexpected sentence behind it.|Cute and mildly strange. An excellent combination.|I'd ask which unusual habit she enjoys most.|A quirk can make affection feel particular to one life.|Perfectly polished gets boring. One odd detail helps.|I'd love to hear about a habit only she notices.''')
add('claude','Route114_Text_ClaudePostBattle','Claude plans to fish at Meteor Falls for something big.',
'''A very grand setting for an optimistic fishing line.|A new habitat may offer different encounters, though size isn't certain.|Watch your footing around the falls.|The sound of the water must make waiting feel different.|He should pack lunch rather than depend on catching dinner.|He has chosen an appropriately spectacular backdrop for hope.|A dramatic location for staring at a small float.|Check access and the current before choosing a casting spot.|Curiosity has drawn him toward water hidden in stone.|He has faith in the location. I hope he has practical shoes.|The falls have already caught his imagination before he's cast a line there.''')
add('ivy','Route114_Text_IvyPostBattle','Ivy learned Pokemon training from her mentor Tyra.',
'''Tyra helped start an adventure with rather a lot of walking.|A patient mentor can make the early lessons less daunting.|Good mentor. Now Ivy can build on it.|It's nice to hear her name the person who helped.|Passing on a skill can change someone else's days.|A shared beginning with room for Ivy's own chapters.|A recommendation that turned into an entire hobby.|I'd ask which first lesson made the biggest difference.|Someone else's kindness can open a path beneath us.|A good mentor gives you room to develop your own style.|I'd like to hear what Ivy enjoys most now.''')
add('kai','Route114_Text_KaiPostBattle','Kai responds to losing by planning a bigger catch.',
'''His next battle plan has been submitted to the river.|A bigger Pokemon would still need a thoughtful training plan.|Bigger isn't always the answer. Worth remembering.|He certainly recovered his enthusiasm quickly.|I hope he likes the next catch for more than its size.|The sequel will apparently have a larger cast member.|Escalation by fishing. A remarkably damp strategy.|I'd review what failed before changing the team's dimensions.|Strength can grow without taking up more space.|An imposing silhouette can't do all the work.|He looks ready to chase the next idea before examining what just happened.''')
add('lenny','Route114_Text_LennyPostBattle','Lenny once thought echoes were someone copying his yodel.',
'''A childhood rival with identical timing and no manners.|An echo can be a convincing surprise before you know its source.|Hard to win an argument with your own echo.|I remember wondering where sounds went after I made them.|That must have made the mountain feel less lonely.|A mysterious duet with an exceptionally unoriginal partner.|An unseen heckler who steals all your best material.|A nice example of sound returning from a distant surface.|The mountain answered him in the only voice it had.|A rival who copied his entire performance. Shameless.|I'd love to hear how he finally worked it out.''')
add('lucas','Route114_Text_LucasPostBattle','Lucas warns of blizzards and avalanches in winter mountains.',
'''The mountain has a winter mood we should take seriously.|Seasonal conditions can change the risks of the same trail.|Check the weather. Turn back when needed.|A familiar path could feel very different under snow.|Warm supplies matter, and so does knowing when to stop.|A beautiful mountain doesn't promise a gentle journey.|A convincing reason to respect the season's boundaries.|Route planning needs current conditions, not just an old map.|Snow can hide more than the shape of the ground.|A scenic trip still needs sensible layers and judgment.|It's useful hearing about the mountain in a season we can't see from here.''')
add('nancy','Route114_Text_NancyPostBattle','Nancy feels sleepy after a tasty meal.',
'''soft_smile~Lunch has cast a very comfortable spell.|A satisfying meal and a quiet rest sound well matched.|Find a good spot before nodding off.|She sounds wonderfully content with the afternoon.|soft_smile~A good meal deserves a few unhurried minutes afterward.|The feast has requested an extended intermission.|An argument for napping with excellent supporting evidence.|Rest somewhere safe rather than letting sleep choose for her.|Fullness can make the whole day feel softer.|She looks like the meal met every expectation.|That sleepy smile is a fairly convincing review of the meal.''')
add('nolan','Route114_Text_NolanPostBattle','Nolan cannot quit because each attempt might succeed.',
'''The next try keeps sending him very persuasive letters.|Anticipation can keep people returning despite uncertain rewards.|Try again if you like. Know when to rest.|I understand wanting one more chance after getting close.|A break doesn't mean abandoning the thing he loves.|Hope has mastered the art of the unfinished sentence.|The next attempt has excellent marketing.|He could track what improves instead of counting attempts alone.|A possibility can tug harder than a certainty.|Persistence is lovely when it leaves room for the rest of life.|He seems to remember the possibility more vividly than the disappointments.''')
add('shane','Route114_Text_ShanePostBattle','Shane enjoys camping with his Pokemon.',
'''A camping party with its own unusual sleeping arrangements.|Sharing quiet routines can strengthen a partnership outside battle.|Good company makes a camp better.|The evening sounds nicer with familiar Pokemon nearby.|I'd enjoy making a camp meal for that little gathering.|An adventure improved by the company between the exciting parts.|A tent full of company and questionable personal space.|I'd ask how he arranges a comfortable camp for all of them.|A temporary home can still hold familiar warmth.|Camping looks better when everybody has somewhere comfortable to settle.|I bet he has small camp memories that matter more than the dramatic stories.''')
add('steve','Route114_Text_StevePostBattle','Steve dreams of a huge Pokemon with horns and fangs.',
'''His dream Pokemon sounds expensive to buy a toothbrush for.|An imposing appearance needn't tell us its temperament.|Big horns mean giving it plenty of room.|I wonder whether it would have some unexpectedly gentle habit.|Feeding a Pokemon that large would require a proper plan.|A formidable outline, awaiting an actual personality.|A lovely nightmare with significant housing requirements.|I'd work out space and care needs before admiring the specifications.|A fierce shape can shelter a surprisingly soft nature.|He has a clear silhouette in mind. Very dramatic taste.|He's imagined the horns very clearly. I'm curious whether he's imagined its personality.''')
add('tyra','Route114_Text_TyraPostBattle','Tyra explains she has been teaching Ivy about Pokemon.',
'''A battle lesson with a very lively demonstration.|Explaining a skill can reveal what we understand about it.|Good to pass it on. Let Ivy try things too.|I hope Ivy feels comfortable asking the little questions.|Teaching kindly can make the first mistakes less scary.|A mentor gets to help someone else find their own story.|An apprenticeship with fewer dusty books than expected.|Hands-on practice can make an explanation much clearer.|A lesson grows when the student can make it their own.|The best guidance leaves room for a personal style.|You can learn a lot about a teacher by how comfortable the student looks beside them.''')
add('alix','Route115_Text_AlixPostBattle','Alix decides to Teleport home.',
'''An exit with absolutely no concern for the return walk.|A convenient journey, assuming a familiar safe destination.|Home sounds good. Convenient way to get there.|I envy being able to skip the awkward walk away.|They can get home while supper is still warm.|A farewell with exceptionally little travel time.|Leaving instantly is a social skill I deeply admire.|Transport without tired feet has obvious advantages.|Some people carry a very short path home.|A dramatic exit that doesn't even scuff the shoes.|I'd barely have time to finish waving goodbye.''')
add('cyndy','Route115_Text_CyndyPostBattle','Cyndy values sand cushioning her training.',
'''The beach has volunteered as a very large cushion.|A softer surface changes impact, though footing still matters.|Soft landing helps. Keep your footing too.|The sand does make every movement look a little different.|A comfortable place to train makes it easier to return.|A training ground with built-in sympathy for mistakes.|A cushion that follows you home in your shoes.|Surface stability matters alongside how well it absorbs impact.|The ground can make practice a little less punishing.|Functional scenery. Shame about getting it out of the clothes.|I'd watch how her steps change compared with firm ground.''')
add('hector','Route115_Text_HectorPostBattle','Hector is satisfied with the rare Pokemon he has.',
'''His wish list has one entry and a very happy checkmark.|Contentment gives him room to learn about the Pokemon he has.|Good. No need to chase everything.|He sounds happy simply being with that one Pokemon.|Knowing what makes you content saves a lot of needless chasing.|A collector who has found a graceful stopping point.|A completed collection of exactly enough.|He can spend attention on care rather than constant acquisition.|Enough can be a surprisingly quiet discovery.|A favorite deserves more attention than an endless shopping list.|He sounds pleased with what he has instead of distracted by what's missing.''')
add('helene','Route115_Text_HelenePostBattle','Helene assumes we must be a Gym Leader because we won.',
'''We won a battle and acquired an imaginary workplace.|Skill alone doesn't establish someone's official position.|Strong trainer doesn't automatically mean Gym Leader.|It's flattering, though a little awkward to answer.|We can thank her without accepting a job we don't have.|A splendid promotion with no interview and uncertain paperwork.|Our victory has caused an administrative misunderstanding.|She might compare our decisions rather than guessing a title.|Strength can belong to people without a sign over their door.|Quite a compliment, wrapped in a bold assumption.|I'd like to hear which part reminded her of a Gym battle.''')
add('jaiden','Route115_Text_JaidenPostBattle','Jaiden wants reassurance that his Pokemon were impressive.',
'''They were ultra. The result was a separate department.|Their strengths can be acknowledged without changing the outcome.|They fought well. He can be proud of that.|He sounds like he wants someone to notice them kindly.|A loss doesn't mean they weren't worth admiring.|The review can contain praise without rewriting the ending.|A score is not a complete personality assessment.|I'd point out something specific they did well.|Their worth didn't leave when the match ended.|Of course there were good details. He deserves a real one.|I'd tell him which Pokemon moment caught my attention.''')
add('koichi','Route115_Text_KoichiPostBattle','Koichi wants to grow stronger with his Machop crew.',
'''A whole crew of enthusiastic reasons to keep training.|Shared practice lets him improve alongside the Machop.|Work with them. Don't just demand more.|He sounds fond of the whole little group.|A team that trains together needs to rest together too.|A determined ensemble with a trainer joining the effort.|His training partners look capable of enforcing attendance.|Coordinating several eager partners takes a clear routine.|Their shared wish gives the work somewhere to go.|He includes himself in the effort. Good leadership.|The way he says crew makes them sound like a group with its own little history.''')
add('kyra','Route115_Text_KyraPostBattle','Kyra blames battling while running then plans another calming run.',
'''Running caused trouble, so she prescribed more running.|Doing two demanding tasks together can divide attention badly.|Stop for the battle next time. Run afterward.|I understand wanting to move after an awkward moment.|A quieter pace might help her recover rather than rush again.|The solution resembles the problem, with one fewer activity.|She has a very consistent escape route.|Separate the tasks and each should become easier to manage.|Movement can settle her, provided she isn't fleeing the feeling.|She could keep the run and lose the multitasking.|I'd like to see her battle when she's standing still.''')
add('marlene','Route115_Text_MarlenePostBattle','Marlene finds this place too busy for meditation with Pokemon.',
'''Her quiet moment has attracted a surprising amount of plot.|The surroundings may not support the kind of focus she wants.|Find a quieter spot. No need to force it.|It's hard to settle when you keep waiting for another interruption.|A small move away from the traffic might help.|Her attempt at stillness has received too many guest appearances.|Peace appears to have chosen another meeting place.|She could look for shelter from both noise and foot traffic.|A place can be beautiful without being right for quiet.|The setting needs to work for her, not just look serene.|She noticed the place wasn't helping. Finding another spot could change the whole afternoon.''')
add('nob','Route115_Text_NobPostBattle','Nob is excited his Pokemon may surpass his karate skills.',
'''He is raising his own very polite competition.|A teacher can take real satisfaction in a student's progress.|Good teacher. Doesn't need to stay ahead forever.|It's lovely that the thought makes him happy.|Passing on a skill is sweeter when you want them to flourish.|The master welcomes a future plot twist at his own expense.|A teacher without a desperate need to remain impressive.|Better results mean his teaching has something working.|A lesson can grow beyond the hand that offered it.|Confidence that leaves space for someone else to shine.|I'd love to see the first technique they do better than him.''')
add('timothy','Route115_Text_TimothyPostBattle','Timothy believes skill comes from effort rather than innate genius.',
'''Convenient. Effort is easier to schedule than being born again.|Practice matters greatly, though people begin with different advantages.|Work counts. Make it useful work.|I like the thought that an awkward beginning isn't the end.|Consistent practice matters more than looking gifted at the start.|A belief that gives the next chapter something to do.|Good. My genius appears to have missed its appointment.|Effort works best with feedback and appropriate rest.|A skill can be grown without arriving fully formed.|The work behind a polished result deserves some attention.|His belief gives beginners a reason to keep trying after an unimpressive start.''')
add('clark','Route116_Text_ClarkPostBattle','Clark treats mountains as roads without needing a tunnel.',
'''He looked at a mountain and saw an unusually tall pavement.|A hiker's route still depends on terrain and conditions.|A route over isn't always a safe route. Check first.|He makes the climb sound less daunting than it looks.|Even the long way needs water and a sensible pace.|A blocked road has merely become a more ambitious road.|An excellent philosophy for someone else's knees.|The direct path isn't the only possible route, but assess both.|A mountain can invite a crossing without promising one.|Confidence is useful when backed by suitable footwear.|He sees a route where I first saw an obstacle. Experience changes the view.''')
add('dawson','Route116_Text_DawsonPostBattle','Dawson complains the battle mussed his Pokemon and his own hair.',
'''The battle has offended two hairstyles simultaneously.|A vigorous battle is unlikely to preserve careful grooming.|Everyone's all right? The hair can wait.|I didn't realize both of them had matching worries.|A brush and a quiet break may solve most of this.|A tragedy in two carefully arranged parts.|The stylist has been summoned to a double disaster.|Some damage reports concern performance; his concerns volume.|A few disturbed strands needn't spoil their whole day.|Battle hair happens. Let's check the Pokemon before the fringe.|I'd be curious what both styles looked like before the match.''')
add('devan','Route116_Text_DevanPostBattle','Devan considers trying different Pokemon types.',
'''His strategy has discovered there are other departments.|Different types can expose him to useful new interactions.|Worth trying. Learn the new partners too.|A different team might help him notice habits he missed.|Variety is useful if everyone gets proper attention.|A change of cast might suggest a different kind of scene.|A type problem is at least easier to name than vague doom.|He can test one change instead of rebuilding everything at once.|A new companion may change more than the battle plan.|Variety works best when the pieces fit together.|He sounds curious again. That's a good change from simply being disappointed.''')
add('janice','Route116_Text_JanicePostBattle','Janice wants Pokemon that combine cuteness and power.',
'''Adorable and formidable. An efficient little package.|Appearance and battle capability needn't be mutually exclusive.|Cute can still hit hard. Fair point.|It's nice when you love their look and what they can do.|I'd add enjoying their company to those requirements.|A charming face is no promise of a gentle contest.|A threat with excellent presentation. I respect it.|Two desired features, with care requirements still worth checking.|Soft appearances can hold considerable strength.|That's a strong combination. Personality completes the look.|The surprise is part of the charm when something adorable turns out to be formidable.''')
add('jerry','Route116_Text_JerryPostBattle Route116_Text_JerryPostRematch','Jerry fears Roxanne will be angry unless he repeats school courses.',
'''The battle has assigned him some surprise homework.|Reviewing a difficult topic is a reasonable response to a setback.|Redo the lesson. No shame in needing another pass.|I hope he can ask for help without feeling embarrassed.|A patient explanation could make the next try easier.|A return to the classroom needn't be written as punishment.|Academic dread has arrived ahead of the report card.|He could identify the missing skill before repeating every course.|A lesson revisited can become clearer, not merely longer.|He needs useful guidance more than an angry review.|He's worrying about Roxanne's reaction before he's had time to understand his own mistake.''')
add('joey','Route116_Text_JoeyPostBattle','Joey proudly collects another bandage as a sign of toughness.',
'''His badge collection is getting unusually adhesive.|Bandages indicate an injury was treated, not how capable he is.|Tough is knowing when to stop getting hurt.|I hope he's less sore than he's pretending.|Taking care of the injury matters more than displaying it.|A souvenir I'd rather he didn't feel obliged to collect.|A terrible reward scheme with excellent sticking power.|Protective habits would be a better measure of progress.|Healing needn't become another test of bravery.|He doesn't need another injury to prove the outfit works.|He's showing the bandage so proudly that it might hide how much the injury bothers him.''')
add('johnson','Route116_Text_JohnsonPostBattle','Johnson asks us to stay and keep him company.',
'''We can stay awhile. I brought at least three words.|A short conversation seems a perfectly reasonable request.|A little while. What's on his mind?|I don't mind quiet company if he's comfortable with that.|We can share a break before getting back on the road.|Not every invitation needs a challenge attached.|I can remain socially present without becoming talkative.|We have time to hear what brought him here.|A brief meeting can soften a lonely stretch of road.|It's nice being asked to stay rather than being tested again.|A familiar road probably looks different after you've watched enough people pass.''')
add('jose','Route116_Text_JosePostBattle','Jose likes Bug Pokemon for their fast evolution.',
'''His team has an unusually efficient growing schedule.|Early evolution can change a team's capabilities quickly.|Quick progress still needs good care.|It must be exciting to see changes arrive so soon.|He'll have plenty of new habits to learn as they grow.|A coming-of-age story with a brisk opening chapter.|A lot of transformation for a very small creature.|He should adjust his plan as their abilities change.|Small beginnings can unfold sooner than we expect.|A dramatic new look delivered ahead of schedule.|Watching a little Bug Pokemon change so quickly must give him plenty to notice.''')
add('karen','Route116_Text_KarenPostBattle','Karen fears she cannot become elegant like Roxanne.',
'''Elegance has survived worse than a single rough battle.|One defeat doesn't determine the kind of trainer she can become.|Keep learning. A loss doesn't cancel the goal.|She can admire Roxanne without matching her immediately.|It's easier to grow when every mistake isn't a verdict.|Even admired trainers had chapters their admirers never saw.|Elegance includes not declaring your entire future ruined.|She could choose one habit of Roxanne's to practice.|A graceful future can begin in an awkward moment.|Borrow the inspiration, not the impossible expectation.|She has a vivid idea of who she admires. I hope she leaves room for her own way too.''')
add('sarah','Route116_Text_SarahPostBattle','Sarah finds wealth cannot buy success with Pokemon.',
'''Her money found a problem it can't pay to leave.|Resources help with care, but cannot replace a relationship or judgment.|Can't buy trust. Have to earn that part.|It must feel strange when the usual answer doesn't work.|Time and attention matter even with the best supplies.|An inconvenient plot for a fortune accustomed to resolving things.|A refreshing failure of the universal shopping strategy.|Expensive tools still need informed use and patient practice.|Some things grow only through being present.|The finest accessories can't make a partnership for her.|This seems to be teaching her something she couldn't simply arrange to be delivered.''')
add('aisha','Route117_Text_AishaPostBattle','Aisha thinks worrying about losing makes loss more likely.',
'''Worry has been accused of helping the other team.|Anxiety can distract, though simply forbidding worry rarely removes it.|Focus on the next move. Easier than policing every feeling.|Worrying about worrying sounds like a difficult extra task.|A small practical step may help more than demanding confidence.|The nervous mind hardly needs a second critic.|Wonderful. Now losing has given anxiety more material.|A clear routine can give attention somewhere useful to go.|A worried person still deserves patience, including from themselves.|Confidence needn't mean never feeling uncertain.|Looking calm and feeling calm can be quite different. The advice needs room for both.''')
add('anna','Route117_Text_AnnaPostBattle Route117_Text_AnnaPostRematch','Anna praises our combinations while calling her team better.',
'''A compliment wearing a tiny competitive hat.|She noticed the combinations, even while protecting her own ranking.|Good combinations. Strange ranking after that result.|The compliment got shy just before reaching us.|We can take the kind part without arguing the rest.|A gracious review with one carefully protected footnote.|Second place has apparently become an honorary title.|The interesting part is which pairings she noticed.|Admiration can arrive carrying a little pride.|She found a way to compliment us without surrendering her image.|She noticed our teamwork even while protecting her pride. I'll keep the kind part.''')
add('brandi','Route117_Text_BrandiPostBattle','Brandi recommends the complexity of Psychic Pokemon.',
'''Complicated company with excellent potential for surprises.|Their capabilities would reward careful study rather than assumptions.|Learn what they need before bringing one along.|A complicated partner might still have simple favorite things.|Understanding them should matter as much as their moves.|An intriguing recommendation with plenty left unexplained.|Complexity is welcome, provided it doesn't read my drafts.|I'd start by observing how they respond in ordinary situations.|An unusual mind still deserves an attentive friend.|Interesting is a good beginning. Compatibility matters too.|She seems drawn to the parts that take time to understand, which is intriguing.''')
add('derek','Route117_Text_DerekPostBattle','Derek reconciles his love of Bug Pokemon with being called a maniac.',
'''He followed his heart and acquired an official-sounding nickname.|Strong interests can produce expertise, even with an exaggerated label.|Knows his bugs. That's the useful part.|It sounds like he's decided the name fits after all.|Loving something deeply isn't a reason to be ashamed.|A title he resisted, then defended with admirable enthusiasm.|Expertise with a slightly alarming business card.|I'd rather hear what he knows than debate the label.|He has found a name for the path he already follows.|Owning the nickname takes some of its sting away.|He talked himself from defending the interest to happily owning the name.''')
add('dylan','Route117_Text_DylanPostBattle','Dylan worries the battle dropped him to last in his race.',
'''His race kept going while his battle took a detour.|Stopping to battle likely changed his position in the race.|Check the course. No use guessing from here.|That sounds like a difficult way to divide his attention.|He should catch his breath before rushing to make it up.|Two competitions, and neither agreed to pause for the other.|An ambitious schedule with competing definitions of winning.|Next time he may want to separate racing from battling.|The road kept moving in his absence.|A busy afternoon needs fewer simultaneous scoreboards.|He keeps looking as if the rest of the race might suddenly appear behind us.''')
add('isaac','Route117_Text_IsaacPostBattle','Isaac values developing Pokemon individuality beyond raw power.',
'''A personality can't be measured with a very large punch.|Individual traits offer ways to engage beyond battle strength.|Know your partner. Not just the damage numbers.|The little differences are often the parts I remember.|Their preferences make caring for them feel personal.|A strong character deserves more than one measurable attribute.|A welcome defense of being interesting rather than intimidating.|A team improves when its particular strengths are understood.|Each life has details no ranking can hold.|A distinctive trait can make a Pokemon unforgettable.|He sounds like someone who notices what makes one Pokemon different from another.''')
add('lydia','Route117_Text_LydiaPostBattle','Lydia advises attention to Pokemon character traits.',
'''The team comes with personalities, not instruction stickers.|Observing individual behavior helps tailor care and training.|Watch what suits them. Don't force one plan on all.|It helps when someone notices the small differences.|Knowing their preferences makes ordinary care much easier.|An attentive author would never give every character the same lines.|A useful reminder that quiet doesn't mean empty.|Different responses suggest different ways to teach.|A companion reveals itself through familiar little choices.|The details distinguish a real personality from a tidy label.|That sort of attention is how a familiar face starts becoming a particular friend.''')
add('maria','Route117_Text_MariaPostBattle','Maria praises regular training then delays it until tomorrow.',
'''Regular training begins at the ever-moving tomorrow.|A routine needs a realistic starting point as well as good intentions.|Tomorrow keeps getting very convenient, doesn't it?|She sounded so determined until the last word.|A small bit today might make tomorrow easier.|A magnificent declaration, followed by a very soft postponement.|My favorite schedule: tomorrow, indefinitely.|A modest task now would make that routine less theoretical.|An intention grows better with a small act attached.|She has the speech ready. The habit needs a fitting.|That final word changed the whole picture rather neatly.''')
add('meg','Route117_Text_MegPostBattle','Meg blames herself for dragging Anna down.',
'''A double battle shouldn't leave one person carrying the whole loss.|Both partners affect a shared result. Blame needs more care than that.|They were a team. So was the loss.|I hope Anna tells her she's more than a mistake.|They can work on the pairing without making Meg the problem.|A partnership deserves a kinder account than one guilty character.|Self-blame is an enthusiastic and unreliable narrator.|Review the interaction rather than declaring one person defective.|A shared effort should leave room for shared kindness.|Meg needs a teammate, not a verdict on her worth.|Meg sees the whole defeat through her own mistake. There must be more to their match.''')
add('melina','Route117_Text_MelinaPostBattle','Melina enjoys jogging while looking at flowers.',
'''A scenic route with a built-in excuse to slow down.|An enjoyable setting can make a routine easier to maintain.|Good view. Still watch where your feet go.|That sounds nicer than staring only at the road.|A pleasant route gives her another reason to get outside.|Exercise with a generous decorative budget.|A lovely distraction with occasional ankle-related consequences.|She gets movement and changing scenery in the same outing.|The flowers give familiar steps a little variation.|A route that changes its colors without needing a new wardrobe.|She has a reason to look forward to the route before the exercise even starts.''')
add('barny','Route118_Text_BarnyPostBattle','Barny wonders if mixing fishing and training weakened both.',
'''His two hobbies have requested separate appointments.|Dividing attention may have limited the feedback from training.|Pick one task and give it a fair try.|Doing both sounds relaxing until each needs you at once.|Some things work better with a little uninterrupted time.|An ambitious double feature with insufficient rehearsal.|Two pleasant pursuits can produce one distracted afternoon.|Separate sessions would help test whether distraction was the problem.|Attention cannot always be shared as evenly as time.|A simpler plan might make both hobbies more satisfying.|He sounds less sure about the arrangement now that he's seen where his attention went.''')
add('chester','Route118_Text_ChesterPostBattle','Chester wants his Pokemon stronger so they can fly freely.',
'''Strength with a very roomy reward: more sky.|Stamina and skill could expand the flights they manage comfortably.|Train steadily. Don't push them past tired.|I like that he pictures what the strength will let them enjoy.|A rested bird will enjoy the practice more.|A goal beyond winning: a larger world for his partners.|A training plan with unusually good views.|Gradual exercise and observation would help him judge their limits.|Freedom can grow from a patient foundation.|He wants them capable, not simply impressive. Nice distinction.|I'd love to see the first flight that surprises him.''')
add('dalton','Route118_Text_DaltonPostBattle','Dalton explains electric guitar can be gentle and moving.',
'''The guitar has more settings than extremely loud, apparently.|The instrument's sound depends greatly on technique and amplification.|Doesn't need to shout to be heard.|Yes. A lightly played electric guitar can sound wonderfully tender.|A gentle tune could change the whole feel of this stop.|Intensity needn't announce itself at maximum volume.|A welcome defense of electricity behaving quietly.|The same equipment can produce very different results in careful hands.|A small sound can carry a feeling a long way.|Restraint gives the details room to stand out.|I'd listen for how he makes one phrase feel different.''')
add('deandre','Route118_Text_DeandrePostBattle','Deandre proudly permits us to copy his battle team idea.',
'''He has generously released the idea of having a team.|His enthusiasm is clearer than the originality of the suggestion.|Kind offer. We already brought a team.|He sounds so pleased that I wouldn't spoil the moment.|We can admire his team without ordering an identical one.|A sweeping license to adopt a fairly established practice.|An invention with suspiciously widespread prior use.|I'd ask what makes his particular team work together.|Pride can make a familiar idea feel newly discovered.|A personal style is more interesting than a straight copy.|He's so pleased with the whole idea that I want to hear about the individual Pokemon.''')
add('perry','Route118_Text_PerryPostBattle','Perry compliments our Pokemon and plans better training.',
'''A compliment and a plan. Efficient use of a loss.|He recognizes the team's quality while identifying work of his own.|Good match. Plenty to build on next time.|He made that sound hopeful rather than defeated.|It's kind of him to notice our team before planning his next try.|An appreciative rival with somewhere to go from here.|A loss that produced neither insults nor a prophecy. Refreshing.|One specific training goal could make his next effort clearer.|He can admire another team without abandoning his own.|A generous compliment looks good on a competitive person.|He turned a compliment to us into encouragement for himself. That's a useful habit.''')
add('rose','Route118_Text_RosePostBattle','Rose likes pleasant-smelling flowers and Pokemon.',
'''Her nose has very firm membership requirements.|Scent is clearly an important part of what she enjoys.|Fair enough. Don't blame a Pokemon for its smell.|Some scents make a place feel familiar immediately.|A pleasant aroma can make a whole room welcoming.|She has an exacting critic working just above her mouth.|My preferences lean toward rain and away from suspicious drains.|I'd ask how she distinguishes the scents she likes.|A fragrance can leave a quiet mark on a memory.|She has a clear preference. Not everything needs her approval.|She probably remembers places by their scents the way I remember their light.''')
add('wade','Route118_Text_WadePostBattle','Wade compares fishing to a battle between fisherman and Pokemon.',
'''A battle with an unusually long opening stare.|There is a contest involved, though the participants differ greatly.|Then keep the Pokemon's condition in mind too.|It must feel different once there's movement on the line.|An encounter should end with care, however exciting the catch.|A duel conducted through a surprisingly thin connection.|A contest where one side didn't read the invitation.|Tension and timing matter, but so does safe handling.|The other end of the line holds a living creature.|Skill includes how gently he handles the end of the contest.|That little line connects two very different views of the same encounter.''')
add('brent','Route119_Text_BrentPostBattle','Brent smugly refuses to explain the appeal of mimicry.',
'''A secret so mysterious it looks exactly like our walking.|He could explain its appeal rather than declaring us incapable.|Fine. He can keep his copying secrets.|Maybe he enjoys the timing more than explaining it.|He's welcome to his hobby. We don't need to argue.|An exclusive mystery with extremely visible supporting evidence.|I'm coping bravely with this alleged lack of understanding.|Coordinated mimicry might be interesting if he discussed the technique.|Some people like a small mystery more than an answer.|That is a lot of exclusivity for something based on copying.|I'd watch what they actually do instead of chasing that boast.''')
add('catherine','Route119_Text_CatherinePostBattle','Catherine praises our efficient travel and readiness.',
'''Light luggage, heavy praise. A favorable exchange.|Preparedness is as much about choosing essentials as carrying more.|Carry what works. Leave room to move.|It's nice when the preparation shows without having to explain it.|A little planning saves tired feet and missed meals.|A rare compliment to the less dramatic parts of an adventure.|Our bag has apparently concealed its chaotic inner life well.|A compact kit is easier to use if everything has a place.|Enough is useful when we recognize it before packing.|Traveling light has a practical elegance of its own.|I'd compare notes on the things she never travels without.''')
add('chris','Route119_Text_ChrisPostBattle','Chris loves surfing on his Pokemon then fishing from its back.',
'''A fishing platform with its own opinions and swimming lessons.|That sounds pleasant if his Pokemon is comfortable with the arrangement.|Make sure his partner gets a break too.|A quiet moment shared out on the water sounds lovely.|He should bring something his Pokemon enjoys afterward too.|Luxury accommodation with an exceptionally devoted host.|A seat that deserves its own thank-you and rest.|Balance and a willing, rested partner seem essential.|He has found a peaceful moment carried by another life.|A lovely outing when both participants enjoy the arrangement.|They must know each other's movements well to make that peaceful moment possible.''')
add('dayton','Route119_Text_DaytonPostBattle','Dayton wants to emulate younger trainers\' enthusiasm.',
'''Pep is contagious. At least it doesn't require a receipt.|Enthusiasm can be borrowed without copying someone else's limits.|Good spirit. Set his own pace.|It's nice that our energy gave him a little of his own.|A fresh burst of enthusiasm can improve an ordinary day.|An inspiring guest appearance by the younger generation.|A much friendlier contagion than most things found outdoors.|He can use the motivation for a manageable new goal.|A lively meeting can stir a familiar path awake.|Energy looks good at any age when it feels natural.|I'd love to hear what he feels like trying next.''')
add('donald','Route119_Text_DonaldPostBattle','Donald impatiently asks us to move so he can mimic us.',
'''He has ordered the next movement from the original supplier.|His practice seems dependent on us providing fresh examples.|We move when we're ready. He can wait.|Being watched so closely makes me forget how walking works.|He can ask without rushing the person he's copying.|An impatient imitator demanding new material from the source.|My next move may be a prolonged, motionless silence.|He could practice recalling a movement instead of demanding another.|Stillness is something he can learn to copy too.|An audience should not be this bossy about the performance.|I'd try a small unexpected gesture and see what he notices.''')
add('doug','Route119_Text_DougPostBattle','Doug introduces the Mimic Circle and hopes we enjoyed it.',
'''A show where we accidentally helped write the choreography.|Matching movement takes attention even when the premise is playful.|Different. They certainly paid attention.|It was a little strange, but the coordination was impressive.|They seem pleased to have shared something they enjoy.|An audience participation piece with unusually thorough participation.|A performance that borrowed my awkwardness with permission pending.|I'd ask how they practice keeping everyone synchronized.|A little shared oddness can brighten the road.|They've built a recognizable group identity. Very coordinated.|They look delighted to share their odd little tradition with someone new.''')
add('fabian','Route119_Text_FabianPostBattle','Fabian demands more music but resents our victory.',
'''He wants an encore and a refund for the same battle.|He sounds caught between enjoying the intensity and disliking the result.|He can have a chord. We still won.|That is quite a lot of frustration packed into a rhyme.|Let him cool down before asking for another round.|A review containing both applause and a demand for reparations.|His rhyme has taken our victory rather personally.|The result won't change because the complaint has rhythm.|A loud feeling needn't decide what happens next.|A dramatic response, with mixed messages in the styling.|I'd wait until he knows whether he wants company or space.''')
add('greg','Route119_Text_GregPostBattle','Greg says the group will mimic us until we leave.',
'''A subscription we cancel by walking out of range.|Their activity ends at a clear geographical boundary, at least.|Then we can leave when we've had enough.|I think knowing when it stops makes it less awkward.|We can give them a wave and keep going.|A very persistent performance with a convenient exit condition.|Excellent. Escape remains part of the rules.|I'd be curious how well they copy a change of pace.|A small step away can end a strangely crowded moment.|Good to know we control how long this look lasts.|I'd like to see whether they all copy the goodbye.''')
add('hideo','Route119_Text_HideoPostBattle','Hideo offers a concealment proverb then denies hidden meaning.',
'''A hidden meaning would clearly hide among other meanings.|Similarity can aid concealment. The second example is rather broad.|No hidden meaning. Plenty of hidden Pokemon, apparently.|He made that sound profound before taking it back.|A practical example might help more than the mysterious delivery.|A proverb followed by a remarkably effective disclaimer.|Depth has been officially excluded from this conversation.|The background needs to match the thing being concealed.|Some sayings are simply odd little stones in the path.|He removed the mystery just after adding the flourish.|His serious delivery made me look for a secret before he told us there wasn't one.''')
add('hugh','Route119_Text_HughPostBattle','Hugh says his Bird Pokemon fulfilled his dream of flying.',
'''A childhood wish with wings and a very good friend.|His partnership opened an experience he couldn't reach alone.|That's a partner worth looking after.|I wonder what the first moment off the ground felt like.|The dream became something they can share together.|A wonderful wish fulfilled without losing the companion behind it.|An uplifting story in the least figurative sense.|I'd ask how they built trust before the first flight.|Someone else's wings have made room for his dream.|The best part is having company in that huge view.|I'd love to hear what he noticed on the first flight.''')
add('jackson','Route119_Text_JacksonPostBattle','Jackson wants to leave civilization and awaken a wild spirit.',
'''His wild spirit should still remember where he packed water.|Leaving familiar routines requires preparation, not only enthusiasm.|Enjoy the wild. Know how to get back.|A quieter life outside town could feel very different.|A wilderness trip still needs meals and a sheltered night.|A grand vision should make room for decidedly practical footnotes.|Civilization does have useful things. Dry socks, for instance.|Test the gear before relying on it far from help.|The wild can welcome attention without promising comfort.|He can embrace the outdoors in clothes that actually work.|He's picturing a whole new version of himself out here. The daily details will shape it too.''')
add('kent','Route119_Text_KentPostBattle','Kent invites us to join the Mimic Circle.',
'''Do I get a membership card, or just copy someone else's?|It might be interesting to try matching their timing briefly.|A short try. Then we've got a road to follow.|I'd feel shy at first, but they seem welcoming.|It's kind of them to invite us into their game.|An invitation to become both performer and surprisingly familiar material.|A social activity with fewer original words required. Tempting.|I'd try a simple sequence before attempting the whole routine.|We can join a small odd moment without staying forever.|A coordinated group could use one delightfully unexpected detail.|I'd enjoy seeing how they welcome a new person.''')
add('phil','Route119_Text_PhilPostBattle','Phil has admired Bird Pokemon since childhood.',
'''A childhood fascination that grew feathers of its own.|A lasting interest can deepen as experience replaces first impressions.|Good to keep something that matters to him.|I wonder which bird he first remembers watching.|Some small childhood joys keep making ordinary days better.|A fondness with a long history and plenty of room left.|An old enthusiasm that still knows how to lift his mood.|I'd ask what he notices now that he missed as a child.|A familiar wonder can remain alive through many seasons.|His taste has consistency without needing to stay unchanged.|That old enthusiasm still changes his expression when he talks about them.''')
add('rachel','Route119_Text_RachelPostBattle','Rachel defends her parasol by pointing at our heavier bag.',
'''Our bag has been called as an inconvenient witness.|She's right that bulk and weight depend on the whole load.|Fair point. Our bag isn't exactly light.|I wasn't trying to criticize. I just wondered.|Her parasol earns its place if it makes the walk nicer.|A pointed rebuttal with excellent supporting luggage.|The bag has chosen a terrible moment to look overstuffed.|We should compare actual weights before judging the design.|Everyone chooses a little comfort worth carrying.|Her accessory serves a purpose. Our bag can stop judging.|She answered the question and spotted the overloaded bag in one very quick glance.''')
add('takashi','Route119_Text_TakashiPostBattle','Takashi acknowledges his surprise attack failed.',
'''The surprise arrived. The victory missed its appointment.|Surprise provides an opening, not a guaranteed result.|An ambush still needs a working follow-through.|He sounds disappointed after all that careful waiting.|He can rest and think about the next attempt.|A dramatic entrance cannot carry the entire scene.|Surprise has limited authority over everything after it.|He could check whether the timing or the plan failed.|A hidden beginning can still lead to an ordinary ending.|The reveal was strong. The rest needs work.|He prepared for our surprise, then found himself surprised by what followed.''')
add('taylor','Route119_Text_TaylorPostBattle','Taylor is frustrated he cannot mimic our victory.',
'''The one thing copying our footsteps couldn't borrow.|Imitating actions doesn't reproduce their entire context or outcome.|Needs his own win. Copying won't supply it.|That must be frustrating after matching everything else.|He could learn from what worked without needing the same result.|The understudy has discovered the ending cannot simply be stolen.|Victory has inconvenient restrictions on duplication.|Understanding the decisions matters more than repeating the motions.|A borrowed shape cannot carry every part of a moment.|A copy can look right and still miss what made it work.|He's reached the part where looking like someone else isn't the same as understanding them.''')
add('yasu','Route119_Text_YasuPostBattle','Yasu quietly withdraws into the shadows after losing.',
'''A dignified exit with excellent natural shade.|He seems ready to reflect without further conversation.|Let him go. The match is finished.|He made the goodbye sound quieter than the forest.|A rest somewhere cool seems reasonable after that.|A restrained ending, which makes a pleasant change.|An exit policy I admire on several personal levels.|He can review the result when he's ready to return.|The shade can hold his silence for a while.|A graceful retreat needs no audience chasing after it.|I'd let the final moment belong to him.''')
add('brooke_rematch','Route111_Text_BrookePostRematch','Brooke wonders if delaying evolution would have taught better moves.',
'''A growth spurt may have overtaken her lesson plan.|Move-learning schedules can differ. She should check the species involved.|Check before regretting it. There may be another way.|I hope she doesn't treat their growing up as a mistake.|She can work with the Pokemon they are now too.|The past is tempting to rewrite when the latest chapter hurts.|A very specific regret. Worth verifying before nurturing it.|Compare the actual move schedules rather than guessing after a loss.|What has grown still deserves her affection.|A new form may need a new approach, not an apology.|I'd ask which move she thinks would have changed the match.''')
add('dusty_rematch','Route111_Text_DustyPostRematch','Dusty\'s uncertainty about his long ruins search expands to fifty years.',
'''Another decade joined while he was counting. Ambitious ruins.|His uncertainty is growing faster than the estimate can settle.|Long search. A notebook might help with the dates.|He remembers the purpose better than the number.|I'd rather hear his favorite discovery than watch him worry.|The chronology has acquired a third competing edition.|Even the estimate is old enough to have its own history.|A first dated note might give that question a firmer starting point.|Time can blur around a place we keep returning to.|His commitment is clearer than the calendar.|I'd ask who he first explored with. That may bring a year back.''')
add('wilton_rematch','Route111_Text_WiltonPostRematch','Wilton recommends aiming for the Pokemon League.',
'''Our next suggested appointment has a very impressive waiting room.|He thinks our present skills justify a larger challenge.|Big goal. We'll prepare before taking it on.|That's encouraging, especially from someone we've battled again.|A challenge that big deserves supplies and a rested team.|A generous recommendation for a considerably larger stage.|A compliment with a formidable amount of homework attached.|We can compare the challenge with what the team handles now.|A distant goal can give familiar steps a direction.|He is taking our progress seriously. That means something.|I'd ask what he thinks we should strengthen before going.''')
add('lao_rematch','Route113_Text_LaoPostRematch','Lao blames his battle skills rather than his concealment.',
'''The hiding received full marks. The battle is retaking the course.|He has separated concealment from what happened after discovery.|Then train the part that failed. Simple enough.|He sounds more certain about what he needs to practice now.|A useful lesson, provided the team gets a break first.|The entrance was flawless; the subsequent scene needs revision.|His camouflage has obtained a written exemption from blame.|Two skills need separate tests. He has identified the weaker one.|Being unseen is only one part of his chosen path.|He has protected his best feature without denying all the work.|I'd ask which battle decision he would change next time.''')
add('madeline_rematch','Route113_Text_MadelinePostRematch','Madeline compliments our continued battle skill.',
'''Our good review has survived the second edition.|She recognizes consistency rather than a single fortunate result.|Kept the standard up. Good to hear.|It feels especially nice when someone remembers how you did before.|She's noticed the work continuing between our meetings.|A returning critic with an encouraging verdict.|Still competent. A modest phrase with impressive staying power.|Repeated results give her impression a stronger basis.|A familiar compliment can gain warmth through being remembered.|She noticed that we kept the quality. Lovely attention to detail.|I'd ask whether she noticed anything different this time.''')
add('steve_rematch','Route114_Text_StevePostRematch','Steve shakes with excitement when watching Pokemon battles.',
'''That battle appears to have reached his entire skeleton.|Excitement can produce a very physical response.|Catch a breath. The fight's over now.|He feels the match much more visibly than I do.|A quiet minute might help him settle after all that.|An audience response with no concern for subtlety.|An enthusiastic review delivered through involuntary movement.|That is a lot of energy to discharge after a match.|Some feelings arrive in the body before words.|His excitement has completely overtaken his composure.|I'd ask which moment gave him that reaction.''')
add('cyndy_rematch','Route115_Text_CyndyPostRematch','Cyndy enjoys battles even when she loses because she loves Pokemon.',
'''soft_smile~Her favorite part was never locked inside the victory.|Enjoyment of the partnership can remain after disappointment.|Good reason to battle. Keep that.|soft_smile~She sounds happy to have spent the time with them.|The team can feel that fondness even after a hard match.|A losing ending hasn't spoiled her entire story.|A hobby with a reward that survives poor results.|That makes practice easier to return to over time.|Affection can make room for an imperfect afternoon.|A person who still likes the experience when it looks untidy.|I'd ask what her Pokemon did that made the battle fun.''')
add('nob_rematch','Route115_Text_NobPostRematch','Nob plans to redouble training to strengthen his Pokemon.',
'''He has ordered a second helping of practice.|More work helps when the method fits the problem.|Train smart. Twice as tired isn't twice as strong.|I hope he leaves room to recover between attempts.|Rest and good meals belong beside the extra practice.|A determined sequel should improve on the method, not just the length.|Double the training sounds suspiciously hard on tomorrow.|I'd check the results before simply increasing the workload.|Growth can need a gentler interval as much as more effort.|Determination works better with a plan that actually fits.|I'd ask what he intends to change besides the amount.''')
add('timothy_rematch','Route115_Text_TimothyPostRematch','Timothy attributes losing entirely to insufficient effort.',
'''Effort is getting blamed for every department now.|A loss may reveal strategy issues as well as insufficient practice.|Work harder if needed. Check the plan too.|I hope he isn't calling every exhausted day laziness.|A rested team can learn more than a worn-out one.|His theory leaves no room for a flawed method.|Effort is a harsh suspect when it has no alibi.|Measure what improved, not simply how long practice lasted.|Devotion needn't become punishment when the result hurts.|The work deserves an honest review, not automatic blame.|I'd ask what he learned rather than how much he suffered.''')
add('karen_rematch','Route116_Text_KarenPostRematch','Karen sees beating Roxanne as beyond her current ability.',
'''She left a little door open with that not yet.|Recognizing a current gap needn't make it permanent.|Not yet is fine. Keep building.|I like that she gave herself room to change.|One step at a time can make the gap less frightening.|A hopeful qualification tucked inside a concession.|Not yet. A surprisingly sturdy pair of words.|She could break that distant standard into smaller skills.|A future does not need to be ready today.|Her confidence left a space for the next version of herself.|I'd ask which lesson from Roxanne she'd practice first.''')
add('dylan_rematch','Route117_Text_DylanPostRematch','Dylan distinguishes athletic confidence from uncertainty with Pokemon.',
'''His confidence arrived wearing the wrong event number.|Experience in one discipline doesn't transfer perfectly to another.|New skill. New practice. He knows how to work.|It's hard starting again when you're used to feeling capable.|He can bring patience from his other training.|A champion elsewhere is still allowed a beginner's chapter.|Competence is inconveniently specific about its travel arrangements.|Some training habits transfer, even when the techniques don't.|He can begin uncertain without beginning empty-handed.|Being good at one thing doesn't require looking polished at all things.|I'd ask which habit from cycling helps him learn now.''')
add('isaac_rematch','Route117_Text_IsaacPostRematch','Isaac recommends Pokemon Contests after praising our team\'s development.',
'''The team has been recommended for a different kind of applause.|Contests could reveal skills a battle doesn't emphasize.|Worth trying if the team enjoys it.|A new kind of performance could feel exciting and a bit scary.|I'd want everyone comfortable before making a big outing of it.|An invitation to discover another side of a familiar cast.|Our progress has earned us additional opportunities to feel awkward.|We should learn the format before designing a routine.|A companion can have more than one way to shine.|A new venue could bring out details people miss in battle.|I'd ask which quality made him think of Contests.''')
add('lydia_rematch','Route117_Text_LydiaPostRematch','Lydia links nature with different Pokeblock preferences.',
'''A team meeting could apparently require several snack bowls.|Individual preferences can make a uniform feeding plan less suitable.|Learn what each one likes. Don't guess for everyone.|It's nice when someone remembers those little differences.|Exactly. Taste a little, observe, and keep track of favorites.|A small preference can give a character surprising definition.|A useful reason not to make everyone share my questionable taste.|Labels and small trials would keep the favorites straight.|What nourishes can also be particular to the one receiving it.|Even snacks have a personal style. I approve.|I'd watch which Pokemon recognizes its favorite first.''')
add('maria_rematch','Route117_Text_MariaPostRematch','Maria again postpones training but invites another battle.',
'''Tomorrow remains the undefeated champion of her schedule.|Her invitation is clear, though the practice date keeps moving.|We'll see her again. Hope tomorrow finally arrives.|She sounds friendly, even if practice still feels far away.|A short session might be easier to start than a grand plan.|A sequel is promised. Preparation remains in development.|Tomorrow has become a suspiciously comfortable hiding place.|She could tie practice to something she already does daily.|A repeated promise may need one small act to give it roots.|The invitation works. The routine could use some structure.|I'd ask what she plans to practice when tomorrow comes.''')
add('meg_rematch','Route117_Text_MegPostRematch','Meg is discouraged that battling with her senior still ended in defeat.',
'''A senior partner isn't a guarantee with legs.|Experience helps, but a partnership still needs coordination.|Both lost. Both can learn from it.|She hoped having Anna beside her would make it feel easier.|They can work on one thing together after a rest.|An experienced partner can guide a chapter without controlling its ending.|Borrowed confidence is still vulnerable to a rough result.|The useful question is how their choices affected each other.|She need not carry the disappointment alone.|They can be a team while they are still figuring things out.|I'd ask which moment they understood each other best.''')
add('dalton_rematch','Route118_Text_DaltonPostRematch','Dalton wants his emotions to reach us through electric guitar.',
'''A message sent through strings instead of the post.|Expression depends on the listener as well as the technique.|Play it honestly. We'll listen.|I'd rather hear what he means than a perfect empty phrase.|A heartfelt tune can make a simple break feel special.|He wants the sound to carry more than the notes alone.|An emotionally revealing conversation with fewer direct questions.|Small changes in touch can change what a phrase conveys.|A feeling can cross a quiet distance without naming itself.|The smallest detail can make an expression feel sincere.|I'd listen, then tell him what stayed with me.''')
add('rose_rematch','Route118_Text_RosePostRematch','Rose explains using sweet aroma to attract Pokemon.',
'''An invitation written entirely for the nose.|Scent can influence encounters, though the response depends on the Pokemon.|Attract them carefully. Give them room.|It must be strange watching something arrive before you hear it.|A pleasant smell can draw company. Kitchens taught me that.|An entrance prompted by an invisible invitation.|The air is doing her recruitment work.|I'd watch the surroundings before setting out the aroma.|An unseen thread can draw a living creature nearer.|Subtle presentation can have a very noticeable effect.|I'd be curious which Pokemon notices the scent first.''')
add('catherine_rematch','Route119_Text_CatherinePostRematch','Catherine reminds us Pokemon rely on their trainer too.',
'''A partnership has two directions. Like a very loyal road.|Dependence is mutual even when each contributes differently.|They trust us. We need to be worth it.|It helps to remember they can feel uncertain too.|Their care shouldn't depend on how useful they were today.|The hero is someone else's supporting character as well.|An uncomfortable amount of responsibility, and a good reason to stay.|A reliable team needs attention to every part, including the trainer.|The hand we lean on may be leaning back.|Being dependable matters more than looking in command.|I'd notice the moments when they look to us for reassurance.''')
add('jackson_rematch','Route119_Text_JacksonPostRematch','Jackson urges trust in Pokemon and self to find the way.',
'''Faith is good luggage. I'd still bring a map.|Confidence helps action, while observation helps choose the route.|Trust the team. Keep your eyes open too.|It's easier to try when you feel you're not doing it alone.|Believing in each other works best with ordinary care behind it.|A stirring line, best accompanied by a few practical directions.|The road can reveal itself before dark, ideally.|A plan gives confidence something concrete to work through.|Trust can steady a step without lighting the whole path.|Confidence should make room for changing course when needed.|I'd ask which experience taught him to trust that way.''')
add('trick_eddie','Route110_TrickHousePuzzle1_Text_EddiePostBattle','Eddie feels more lost after losing inside the Trick House.',
'''The house has doubled his confusion without adding any rooms.|A setback can disrupt the landmarks he was keeping in mind.|Start with where he last knew the way.|It's harder to think when you're embarrassed and turned around.|A pause might help before choosing another corridor.|A maze within a maze, with disappointment doing the remodeling.|Lost in two senses. An unnecessarily efficient building.|Trace the last few turns before adding new ones.|A familiar point can steady a place that feels tangled.|He needs directions more than another review of the battle.|I'd ask which doorway he remembers passing last.''')
add('trick_robin','Route110_TrickHousePuzzle1_Text_RobinPostBattle','Robin asks who we are after seeing our strength.',
'''An ordinary visitor with an unusually eventful afternoon.|The battle gave an impression, but not much of an introduction.|Just another trainer finding the way through.|We could start with our names. That might be easier.|A friendly introduction is a nice change after a match.|A mysterious stranger, if one ignores our perfectly ordinary greeting.|An excellent question I prefer answering without a grand title.|Our next useful fact is probably which route we've checked.|A name can make a sudden encounter feel less strange.|A strong impression still needs a proper introduction.|I'd introduce us and ask what brought Robin here.''')
add('trick_sally','Route110_TrickHousePuzzle1_Text_SallyPostBattle','Sally never tires of cutting obstacles.',
'''She has found a hobby this house is eager to supply.|Repeated work is easier when the task itself is satisfying.|Watch what she's cutting. Not everything's an obstacle.|She sounds wonderfully pleased to have more to do.|A break is still allowed, even when the work is fun.|The scenery has met an enthusiastic editor.|A forceful approach to interior decoration.|A sharp tool needs attention even during familiar work.|Clearing a path can be satisfying without clearing everything.|I hope her enthusiasm distinguishes barriers from furnishings.|I'd ask whether she's found the route she's actually trying to clear.''')
add('trick_georgia','Route110_TrickHousePuzzle2_Text_GeorgiaPostBattle','Georgia thinks we may be strong enough to be a Gym Leader.',
'''A puzzle outing with an unexpected promotion opportunity.|Our battle skill impressed her enough to suggest a much larger role.|Kind compliment. A Gym is a lot of responsibility.|That is flattering, though I wasn't expecting it here.|Looking after challengers would involve more than winning.|A grand title offered in a rather peculiar interview room.|Our application apparently consisted of getting lost and winning.|Running a Gym would require a different set of skills too.|A compliment can open a future without deciding it.|She sees promise. We can accept that without choosing a uniform.|I'd ask what she thinks makes a good Gym Leader.''')
add('trick_paul','Route110_TrickHousePuzzle2_Text_PaulPostBattle','Paul says the Trick Master constructed every mechanism himself.',
'''One man looked at an ordinary house and found it insufficiently confusing.|Designing and installing all of this is a substantial undertaking.|Lot of work. Hope he checks it properly.|It must feel strange living inside all these ideas.|I wonder whether he remembered a normal place to eat.|A singular vision, expressed through an unreasonable number of obstacles.|A home improvement project that turned against its visitors.|All by himself? I'd love to understand the moving linkages.|One person's odd thoughts can become a place others walk through.|The commitment to a theme is certainly thorough.|I'd ask how long each redesign takes him.''')
add('trick_ted','Route110_TrickHousePuzzle2_Text_TedPostBattle','Ted asks us to push all the buttons for him.',
'''He has found the outsourcing button. It's us.|He would learn more by tracking what each button changes.|We can help. He still needs to learn the route.|I could show one, then let him try the next.|Working it out together sounds better than doing it all for him.|A clever delegation, though it rather abandons the puzzle.|I admire the honesty of this attempt to avoid homework.|Let's identify the mechanism before pressing everything blindly.|A little guidance can leave him with his own discovery.|Help is fine. Becoming his personal button service is less appealing.|I'd ask which buttons he's already tried and what happened.''')
add('trick_alan','Route110_TrickHousePuzzle3_Text_AlanPostBattle','Alan wonders how many traps the house contains.',
'''The answer might be one more than anyone wants.|Counting mechanisms is harder when the route conceals some of them.|Enough to watch our step. That's my count.|I'd rather find the safe way than every single trap.|We should take the route slowly instead of chasing a total.|A house with an extravagant commitment to complications.|I prefer numbers that don't increase beneath my feet.|A map marking each mechanism would turn guesses into evidence.|The house seems fond of keeping one thing out of sight.|The designer clearly believes more is more.|I'd ask which trap has been hardest for him to spot.''')
add('trick_justin','Route110_TrickHousePuzzle3_Text_JustinPostBattle','Justin feels trapped among cramped dark doorways.',
'''He needs a way out, not another surprise door.|Let's establish a familiar exit before testing more passages.|Stay with him. Find the way back calmly.|That tight dark space sounds genuinely frightening to him.|We can slow down and help him reach somewhere open.|A distressed guest deserves directions, not more theatrical suspense.|The house has exceeded his recommended daily darkness.|Mark a starting point and check one doorway at a time.|A little clear space may help his breathing settle.|We can stop treating this as entertainment for a moment.|I'd ask which way he entered and walk back with him.''')
add('trick_martha','Route110_TrickHousePuzzle3_Text_MarthaPostBattle','Martha calls herself weak and directionless.',
'''Two rough moments don't make a complete description of her.|Navigational difficulty and battle results are separate skills to work on.|Needs a route, not another insult from herself.|She sounds frustrated enough to make every problem feel personal.|A calm break and a little help could change the whole afternoon.|An unkind narrator has taken control of her introduction.|Being lost isn't a character flaw. It's common in here.|A simple map could solve one problem immediately.|A tangled place needn't decide what she is capable of.|She can accept help without making herself the joke.|I'd start by asking where she actually wants to go.''')
add('trick_cora','Route110_TrickHousePuzzle4_Text_CoraPostBattle','Cora assumes trainers will travel anywhere for a battle.',
'''Somewhere in that rule, this house got permission to exist.|Motivation varies. Curiosity can draw people as strongly as competition.|A good battle helps. A safe exit helps too.|Sometimes I just want to see what a strange place is like.|I'd also travel for a good meal. The battle is optional.|A powerful recruitment theory for extremely inconvenient venues.|I reserve the right to avoid certain basements.|Interesting opponents are one reason to explore, not the only one.|Some paths matter for what lies between the challenges.|A place needs more than a guest list to win me over.|I'd ask whether she came for the trainers or the puzzles.''')
add('trick_paula','Route110_TrickHousePuzzle4_Text_PaulaPostBattle','Paula wonders whether anyone has reached the end.',
'''The end is doing an excellent job of avoiding introductions.|We'd need a completed route or a returning visitor to know.|We'll keep looking. No sense guessing.|It would be reassuring to hear from someone who got through.|A quick rest might make the next attempt less frustrating.|The ending has become the house's most elusive character.|A reasonable question for a building this committed to delay.|Someone could record a confirmed route rather than another rumor.|Not seeing the end yet doesn't mean there isn't one.|I would appreciate an exit with a little more visibility.|I'd ask how far she's managed and compare what we've seen.''')
add('trick_yuji','Route110_TrickHousePuzzle4_Text_YujiPostBattle','Yuji says puzzles need thought rather than brute force.',
'''The walls have declined our application to solve them by flexing.|A mechanism rewards understanding of its constraints.|Use your head. Preferably without hitting the wall.|It's nice when stopping to think is the useful move.|A quiet moment can save a lot of wasted effort.|The plot will not advance merely because someone strains impressively.|An argument for thinking that my arms enthusiastically support.|Yes! Figure out the moving parts before applying more force.|A patient look can open what a shove cannot.|Elegance often begins where unnecessary effort stops.|I'd ask what clue changed the way he looked at the room.''')
add('trick_benny','Route110_TrickHousePuzzle6_Text_BennyPostBattle','Benny admits trying to cheat contributed to his defeat.',
'''His shortcut has taken him directly to an awkward explanation.|Cheating also prevented him from testing his actual approach.|Then try it straight next time.|At least he admitted it instead of blaming someone else.|A fair attempt will tell him more about what to practice.|The clever scheme has supplied its own unfavorable ending.|A bad plan with an unusually honest postscript.|A valid attempt gives useful feedback. This one compromised the test.|He can leave the trick behind and begin again plainly.|Owning the mistake is a better look than defending it.|I'd ask what he would try without the shortcut.''')
add('trick_sebastian','Route110_TrickHousePuzzle6_Text_SebastianPostBattle','Sebastian wonders if our calm appearance hides a poker face.',
'''My face often forgets to file the full emotional report.|Outward expression is an imperfect measure of internal response.|Calm face doesn't mean we missed anything.|Sometimes I look quiet because I don't know what to say.|We can be having a busy day without displaying every part.|A composed expression leaves plenty of room for a complicated narrator.|My face isn't a public noticeboard. Usually.|He'd get better information by asking what we noticed.|Still water can hold more than its surface shows.|A reserved look can be natural, not a calculated performance.|I'd tell him what surprised us rather than make him guess.''')
add('trick_sophia','Route110_TrickHousePuzzle6_Text_SophiaPostBattle','Sophia enjoys repeating the Trick House challenge.',
'''She found a house worth getting confused in twice.|Repeating a challenge can reveal details missed the first time.|Good sign. She likes the work, not just finishing.|Familiar puzzles might feel comfortable in a strange way.|An outing you want to repeat is a good discovery.|A peculiar story with genuine rereading value.|She has formed a surprisingly healthy relationship with frustration.|A second pass is perfect for testing a more efficient route.|A place can stay interesting after it stops being unknown.|Some designs reward another look. This one certainly demands one.|I'd ask what she notices on a return visit that others miss.''')
add('trick_alexis','Route110_TrickHousePuzzle7_Text_AlexisPostBattle','Alexis senses we are solving every Trick House puzzle.',
'''Our confusion must be looking impressively productive.|She may be noticing the progress our earlier attempts made.|Working on it. One room at a time.|It's nice to hear that we look more certain than I feel.|A little progress at a time still gets us through.|The audience suspects a competent protagonist. How encouraging.|Our stubbornness has been mistaken for a master plan.|Each solved mechanism gives us better clues for the next.|The way can become clearer through walking it carefully.|Apparently our persistence is making a strong impression.|I'd ask what makes her think we're getting them all.''')
add('trick_alvaro','Route110_TrickHousePuzzle7_Text_AlvaroPostBattle','Alvaro celebrates two odd people meeting in a strange place.',
'''laughing~Two weirdos met in a weird house. Very efficient hospitality.|An unusual setting can make an introduction easier to remember.|Strange place. Decent company. Works for me.|soft_smile~It's easier to relax when someone admits this is a little odd.|A friendly person can make a confusing outing worthwhile.|A fine setting for a friendship nobody could call predictable.|soft_smile~A social category I can join without falsifying my application.|Shared curiosity is a perfectly good reason to get acquainted.|A peculiar place has given us an ordinary kindness.|He made being unusual sound welcoming. I like that.|I'd enjoy hearing what drew his particular kind of weird here.''')
add('trick_everett','Route110_TrickHousePuzzle7_Text_EverettPostBattle','Everett hoped winning would let him switch places with us.',
'''He nearly invented a very competitive moving service.|A desired position is not a substitute for understanding the route.|Didn't work. He'll need another way through.|He sounds like he hoped we could solve being stuck for him.|We can explain the path without turning it into a prize.|A positional plot twist defeated by the actual battle.|A complicated way to request a more convenient location.|He might find a direct route once we compare the mechanisms.|A better place can be reached without taking someone else's.|An ambitious shortcut with rather fragile conditions.|I'd ask where he wants to be and what blocks the way.''')
add('trick_joshua','Route110_TrickHousePuzzle7_Text_JoshuaPostBattle','Joshua wishes he could appear and vanish like smoke.',
'''A useful skill for leaving conversations before the awkward part.|Smoke-like movement is an intriguing wish, though rather difficult to reproduce.|Quick exits sound useful. Keep a solid landing.|I'd enjoy being able to leave quietly without anyone staring.|It would make surprise arrivals a little too easy in the kitchen.|An entrance and exit freed from the tyranny of doors.|A social technique I have been trying to master for years.|I'd first ask what effect makes the disappearance look convincing.|A little smoke has inspired a very human wish.|A dramatic silhouette that takes itself away. Stylish.|I'd ask whether he wants the surprise or the freedom most.''')
add('trick_mariela','Route110_TrickHousePuzzle7_Text_MarielaPostBattle','Mariela insists she is not upset.',
'''The announcement sounds slightly more upset than advertised.|Her words and tone may not be reporting the same thing.|Fine. No need to press the point.|She can have the feeling without explaining it to us.|A little space might be kinder than trying to catch her out.|An emphatic denial with an exceptionally expressive delivery.|I respect the right to be privately furious in public.|We can let things settle instead of demanding a better report.|A feeling does not need to confess before it can pass.|No need to expose the mood she's trying to cover.|I'd change the subject rather than challenge her expression.''')
add('trick_patricia','Route110_TrickHousePuzzle7_Text_PatriciaPostBattle','Patricia blames bad fortune for circling one spot repeatedly.',
'''That spot has become a very persistent acquaintance.|A repeated route suggests a mechanism or choice pattern worth examining.|Mark the turn. Try something different.|Going around again must make it hard to trust her bearings.|A pause could help before walking the same loop hungry.|The scene has repeated enough times to justify a rewrite.|Ill fortune has suspiciously consistent floor plans.|Track the sequence once. A repeated input may explain the loop.|A familiar circle can open when one small step changes.|Ten visits is enough to call the place a bad habit.|I'd ask which turn she keeps choosing without thinking.''')
add('trick_keira','Route110_TrickHousePuzzle8_Text_KeiraPostBattle','Keira calls our victory miraculous and permits us to brag.',
'''A miracle with official bragging authorization. Very generous.|She found the result surprising enough to frame as exceptional.|No need to brag. The win happened.|I'd rather remember the match than make her hear about it all day.|We can enjoy winning without making her the punchline.|A glowing review delivered in an unusually self-protective wrapper.|I may keep the miracle and decline the announcement.|I'd prefer to know which part of the plan surprised her.|An unexpected result needn't become a public trophy.|Permission accepted. Discretion remains the better accessory.|I'd tell the story with her good moves included too.''')
add('trick_leroy','Route110_TrickHousePuzzle8_Text_LeroyPostBattle','Leroy thinks our progress will please the Trick Master.',
'''The house's owner may be delighted we survived his hospitality.|A designer can learn a great deal from a capable participant.|Good. Maybe he'll provide an uncomplicated exit.|It's nice if our effort means something to the person who built this.|I hope he's as pleased when visitors ask for a rest.|The author may finally meet a reader who survived every footnote.|We have supplied valuable data about confusing stubborn people.|I'd love to compare the intended solution with what we actually did.|A strange creation has found someone willing to follow its path.|A good design should welcome people who really engage with it.|I'd ask what reaction the Trick Master usually hopes to see.''')
add('trick_vincent','Route110_TrickHousePuzzle8_Text_VincentPostBattle','Vincent is astonished we defeated the League Champion.',
'''That title does tend to make an introduction rather large.|A major victory can change how someone interprets a later battle.|Still the same trainer standing here.|It's a big thing to hear said aloud in this odd little room.|There was a lot of ordinary care behind that extraordinary day.|A rather significant chapter has entered this peculiar conversation.|An intimidating credential, currently wandering through a puzzle house.|Even that achievement came from solving one problem at a time.|A great moment can travel quietly with the person who lived it.|A grand reputation doesn't stop us getting dusty like everyone else.|I'd rather tell him about the match than just repeat the title.''')
add('institute_grunt1','Route119_WeatherInstitute_1F_Text_Grunt1PostBattle','An Aqua grunt claims the boss knows everything while admitting ignorance.',
'''annoyed~A very confident organization with a remarkably uninformed spokesperson.|His certainty about the boss exceeds the evidence he can explain.|annoyed~Doesn't know the plan. Still chose to help.|He sounds less certain once he talks about his own part.|Not knowing doesn't erase what he's doing to the people here.|An omniscient leader, according to a narrator with no information.|A blank page defending the brilliance of the whole book.|Blind confidence is a poor substitute for understanding the objective.|Obedience can move a hand without answering its conscience.|That defense has impressive posture and very little substance.|I'd pay attention to what he actually did, not his praise of the boss.''')
add('institute_grunt4','Route119_WeatherInstitute_1F_Text_Grunt4PostBattle','An Aqua grunt fears reprimand and wants a nap in an Institute bed.',
'''annoyed~His plan has gone from taking over to taking a nap.|Fear of reprimand doesn't justify using someone else's workplace as a refuge.|annoyed~Leave the staff's beds alone. Go.|He sounds worried, but the people here deserve their space back.|Those beds are for people who belong here and need rest.|A failed invasion has developed an interest in the guest facilities.|The audacity is almost restful in its consistency.|Withdrawal would be a better next step than settling in.|His discomfort does not outrank the lives he interrupted.|An unwelcome guest shouldn't start reviewing the bedding.|I'd rather see him leave than make himself comfortable.''')
add('institute_grunt2','Route119_WeatherInstitute_2F_Text_Grunt2PostBattle','An Aqua grunt wants the Institute\'s weather-changing Pokemon.',
'''annoyed~He heard remarkable Pokemon and immediately skipped to stealing.|A Pokemon's unusual capability doesn't entitle them to control it.|annoyed~It's not theirs. End of argument.|They speak about it as though it couldn't have needs of its own.|The Pokemon deserves care, not a place in their scheme.|A living creature reduced to a convenient device in their plot.|Their sense of entitlement seems entirely weatherproof.|annoyed~A powerful capability makes responsible care more important, not less.|A life is not a prize for whoever wants it most loudly.|Calling it necessary doesn't make taking it acceptable.|I'd listen to the people who actually care for it here.''')
add('institute_grunt3','Route119_WeatherInstitute_2F_Text_Grunt3PostBattle','An Aqua grunt angrily says we do not understand their goals.',
'''annoyed~A secret plan is apparently also an excuse to be rude.|He offers no explanation that would justify the disruption here.|annoyed~Their goals don't excuse hurting people.|We understand enough to see that the staff need help.|A good purpose should survive a question about the people affected.|The villain protests that the audience hasn't read his private notes.|A demand for trust delivered with threats. Unconvincing.|An objective needs scrutiny precisely when its methods cause harm.|A hidden purpose cannot erase a visible wrong.|annoyed~He could explain himself. Instead he chose intimidation.|I'd judge what they're doing in this room before their claims.''')
add('institute_grunt5','Route119_WeatherInstitute_2F_Text_Grunt5PostBattle','An Aqua grunt cryptically insists their real objective is elsewhere.',
'''A mysterious elsewhere still doesn't explain occupying this building.|His vague claim supplies no verifiable information about their aim.|Then leave. Nobody invited them here.|He seems to enjoy knowing something he won't explain.|If they don't need this place, they can stop troubling the staff.|A retreat disguised as exclusive knowledge of the next chapter.|An impressive amount of laughter around an empty explanation.|We should focus on securing this place rather than guessing his riddle.|A cryptic answer can be a way of avoiding a plain responsibility.|The mystery isn't flattering enough to excuse the behavior.|I'd remember the words without pretending they tell us the whole plan.''')
